export const EVENT_BACK = {
  city: {
    1: [[{"n":"The link reattaches easily and the armor is loaded into the back of the transport carriage. The curators thank you profusely for your perceptiveness and are sure to put in a good word with their sponsors.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Gain 10 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"The steel link has softened with age, and you're able to bend it to nicely fit around your finger. It feels somehow right to bring a piece of a legendary warrior's armor back into battle, albeit on a smaller scale.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","If a character owns \"Steel Ring\" 102, they gain 15 gold. Otherwise, gain the \"Steel Ring\" 102 item."]}]],
    2: [[{"t":["persuasive"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive","n":"You give a broad smile to the Savvas and lay out why the businessman's offer would be an excellent opportunity. \"It sounds much more reasonable coming from you than that block-headed businessman. I'll sign.\"","e":["Gain 30 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to convince the Savvas, but it refuses outright. \"I already told that ninny I'm not going anywhere! Find some other old rock to bother.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}],[{"t":["intimidating"],"c":"Trait: Intimidating","n":"The Savvas attempts to slam the door in your face, but you push inside. You start plucking a collection of vases off the wall and \"accidentally\" dropping them. \"Stop! Stop! I'll sign! You monsters.\"","e":["Gain 30 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"Get off my property!\" You try to force your way inside, but the Savvas effortlessly conjures a gust of wind that knocks you back into the street.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Scenario: suffer 1 damage"]}],[{"n":"Let the Savvas stonewall the businessman some more. You report that your negotiation was a failure and take the payment without doing a lick of work.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}]],
    3: [[{"e":["Read section 63.2."]}],[{"t":["educated"],"c":"Trait: Educated","n":"Watching carefully, you deduce there must be a series of mirrors that reflect the blade handles despite appearing to pierce through. You discuss it later at the Sleeping Lion and are pleased you figured it out.","e":["Each character gains 5 XP"]},{"o":1,"n":"You watch the blades go in, the blades come out, and the volunteer emerges unharmed. Even after everything you've seen on the battlefield, this? This is clearly true magic. You erupt in applause.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    4: [[{"n":"You were paid for protection, and you're as good as your word. It takes just a shift in your stance, and the crossbow bolt intended for the nobleman hits you instead.","e":["Select one character to permanently decrease their maximum hit point value by 1 and gain hero. Note both on their character sheet now, then read section 27.1."]}],[{"n":"You cry out before the impact, but it's no use: the crossbow bolt finds its mark dead-center in the nobleman's chest. He slumps to the ground and is dead long before help arrives. The assassin uses the commotion to slip away.\n\nIt's a good thing you always ask for payment up front.","e":["Each character gains 10 gold","Lose 1 reputation with any two factions of your choice."]}]],
    5: [[{"n":"If someone offers you 50 gold, you take 50 gold. The transaction is very simple and doesn't even require paperwork. It's apparently a family business and they'll just keep track and remind you about interest payments as needed.\n\n\"Pleasure getting you signed up, here's your new money.\" The Vermling hands over a pouch that looks less impressive than you expected. \"Bonecruncher will let you know when it's time to collect. Until then, just live it up!\"\n\n...Bonecruncher?","e":["Gain 50 collective gold","Event card city 44","Gain trait: Indebted"]}],[{"n":"It takes some repetition, but you finally make clear you're not going to take this mysterious, anonymous loan. When he hears the finality in your voice, he shrugs, dropping the smarmy smile. He throws a few coins on the table for his drink and leaves the Sleeping Lion without another word.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    6: [[{"n":"A knife makes quick work of the silk ropes tying the man down, and you help him to his feet. He's badly bruised and in no condition to run, but you still keep a firm grasp on him. All it takes is a smile to the unsuspecting guards and you're in the clear. True to his word, he pulls a small glimmering earring out of his pocket and hands it to you.\n\n\"I knew you were like me. Good working with you. And watch out for that green psycho, they're everywhere these days.\"","e":["Gain item 36 Moon Earring"]}],[{"n":"You alert the passing patrol and they quickly apprehend the criminal.\n\n\"Another one by the Green Carapace. Third this week, don't know when this guy has time to sleep.\" The other guard answers quickly: \"They're a Harrower, I don't think they need to sleep. Tell you what, though, I appreciate their help. Somebody needs to smack some sense into these thieves.\"\n\nThere's a small bounty for the criminal, and it doesn't look like the Green Carapace is going to show up to collect it. The guards hand it over to you in thanks.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Military"]}]],
    7: [[{"n":"You attempt to provide an even-handed response about the importance of both aspects of civic life, but the true test of a city is not how it threatens its populace, but how it supports their opportunities to better their own lives.\n\n\"Thank you, mercenaries, for such a compelling argument. I think we'd all agree that, without a vibrant market for goods and services, a city is little more than a transient police state.\" Councilman Greymare looks pleased. By the nods, it's clear the listeners have been hearing only the aspects that support their own arguments. Politicians.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"n":"You attempt to provide an even-handed response about both aspects of civic life, but the true test of a city is whether it can defend its borders and its people against threats to their lives. Livelihoods are necessarily secondary to this primary government goal.\n\nCouncilwoman Vale gives the faintest hint of a smile. \"Truer words have not been spoken, mercenaries. Your city thanks you for your contributions both in oration today and in your own efforts to defend Gloomhaven.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military"]}]],
    8: [[{"n":"Read the section below corresponding to the ancestry of the selected character."},{"t":["orchid"],"c":"Trait: Orchid","e":["section 59.1."]},{"t":["valrath"],"c":"Trait: Valrath","e":["section 9.3."]},{"t":["inox"],"c":"Trait: Inox","e":["section 32.3."]},{"t":["savvas"],"c":"Trait: Savvas","e":["section 132.2."]},{"t":["vermling"],"c":"Trait: Vermling","e":["section 135.2."]},{"t":["quatryl"],"c":"Trait: Quatryl","e":["section 112.5."]},{"t":["harrower"],"c":"Trait: Harrower","e":["section 61.2."]},{"t":["aesther"],"c":"Trait: Aesther","e":["section 124.4."]},{"t":["human"],"c":"Trait: Human","e":["section 91.4."]},{"o":1,"e":["section 105.1."]}]],
    9: [[{"rp":["military",6],"c":"Reputation with Military above 6","n":"\"I am pleased by your readiness to wield such a device, as many do not have the stomach for war. All of my endeavors in this life are in pursuit of greater peace for Gloomhaven.\" She tilts her head in acknowledgment, and you can't help but feel a sense of pride. \"If you will champion such a cause in the defense of Gloomhaven, I would expect nothing less than your service in its use.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Unlock scenario 88"]},{"o":1,"n":"She raises an eyebrow. \"If it is as dangerous as the legends claim, it will be best managed in the hands of those loyal to the city.\" There's no question that she's sizing up your trustworthiness. \"Prove yourself and I will consider your request.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 88"]}],[{"n":"\"As the city's armory is the finest collection of materials for war, it is no surprise to hear your request. I'll see to it that First Shield Harmon permits you access.\"","e":["Collectively gain any one item from 001-014.","Unlock scenario 88"]}]],
    10: [[{"n":"Not entirely sure of the protocol, you attempt to mime acceptance at Sunny. Sunny holds out a sun-drenched hand in response, focusing the energy to a singular point and deftly slicing the display into something new: a diorama of a sword. It returns to a resting position, eyeing you closely without apparent emotion. Xain closes his eyes and touches the miniature.\n\n\"Sunny says it knows how to make some kind of fancy sword with the forge. Get the bugs out, and Sunny will use the facility to sinter it for you.\" Xain's eyes pop open, and he looks grumpily at Sunny. \"You're giving away the sword? Then you and I need to rework our arrangement.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 99"]}],[{"t":["orchid"],"c":"Trait: Orchid","n":"You ask Sunny a series of questions with Xain out of the room. It responds with intricate dioramas, and by touching each, you can tease out the meaning of the psychic patterns that created them. You gather that Sunny met Xain after being trapped in his belt buckle, a story which doesn't get elaborated on. The two formed an unlikely alliance when Xain offered to help clear the Sintering Forge in exchange for using the manufacturing facilities. Xain impatiently returns to the room. \"Well?\"","e":["Each character gains 10 XP","Apply outcome A"]},{"o":1,"n":"With Xain out of the room, you attempt to communicate with the Sun Demon. Sunny melts many objects from around the room into dioramas, but you can't make sense of any of them. Xain returns after a few minutes, exasperatedly surveying the destruction. \"Well, this looks productive. Ready to help?\"","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle","Apply outcome A"]}]],
    11: [[{"n":"\"Thank you for your understanding. My poor friend will not cause such trouble again.\" The portly man places his cloak protectively over his charge, disappearing into the night.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You help the nearly-drowned teen to his feet. The portly man steps forward, \"I assure you, there is no reason for alarm—\" he reaches out to grab the teen, and you shove him to the ground, splashing him into the muddy runoff. He dabs his face with a black handkerchief, and with a dramatic clearing of his throat rushes off to somewhere without another word.\n\nNo sooner than he's out of sight than the teen seems to come out of his daze. \"Thank you, I was telling that man about the Sect when I started feeling winded... then everything got cloudy. I could've sworn he said the word 'sacrifice' right before everything went black.\" He shakes his head, pushing away whatever he has the displeasure of recalling. \"The Sect is doing such important work, I feel the need to tell any who will listen. I don't want... thank you. I don't know where I'd be without you.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Demons"]}]],
    12: [[{"n":"You stretch out and throw the lever down. Down is up and up is, oh, wow, do you feel sick. But at least the sky is where is should be. Now if it would just stop moving.\n\nThe Quatryl, choking back a gag, addresses the crowd sheepishly. \"Sorry, sorry, that... oh wow, that really was turned up much too high. But—but think about how potent it is!\" The crowd doesn't seem impressed.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You stretch out and throw the lever up. Unfortunately, what you believe to be the direction you want to push the lever is so, so wrong. With a lurch, the machine turns on even stronger, sending the gathered crowd reeling. When the Orchid finally gets control of her machine, no amount of apologies will make up for the distress of the crowd, and she packs up and scurries off as quickly as her still-wobbly legs will let her.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]}],[{"n":"There's no mistaking the feeling of relief, but the results wind up all over the machine. With a gurgle, it stops all at once.\n\n\"My machine! It just needed some tweaking...\" You continue on your way rather than stick around to be berated, confident you made the right decision.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    13: [[{"n":"The crowd parts as you approach the dock with weapons drawn. You step onto the soft wood and the Lurkers turn toward you and stop clacking. They all hiss and brandish their claws in aggression. You charge forward and meet the threat head-on, hacking away at their carapaces until they scuttle off the dock and back into the water.","e":["Each character gains 10 XP"]}],[{"n":"The crowd parts as you move toward the dock with both confidence and care. The Lurkers notice your approach and continue to clack in your direction. You call out to them and ask why they are here, but all you get in response is a change in tempo of their clacking. When you express confusion, they clack again in frustration and scuttle back into the ocean. The crowd is very impressed that you managed to ward off the creatures without using force.","e":["Gain 2 reputation with any one faction of your choice."]}]],
    14: [[{"n":"\"Ah, this is a Pinter Droman original! May it never explode, unless you need it to explode, in which case may it explode spectacularly.\"","e":["Gain a random item design","Immediately gain the item from the random item design.","Unlock scenario 87"]}],[{"n":"\"Certainly, please, take your time. They're all equally useful, I assure you. I'm just a bit pinched on gold at the moment, so I can't build everything that comes to mind myself.\" You sort through the blueprints and scrawled diagrams and narrow it down to a few that look promising.","e":["Draw 3 random item designs and choose 1, returning the other 2 to their deck.","Unlock scenario 87"]}]],
    15: [[{"e":["Read section 75.4."]}]],
    16: [[{"c":"Pay 10 collective gold","n":"You step in and pay for the Sect member's purchase before the store owner can raise the alarm. \"You shouldn't help them. Monstrous people, those Sect members. I heard they're trying to summon Demons right into Gloomhaven. They needle you to join their cult one day, and then, the next, they're ripping you off with this filthy scrap. I wish the market would ban them entirely, let them shop in the Sinking Market with the rest of the detritus. Do you want this?\"\n\nYou take the bag of coins to a dealer in the Coin District, whose eyes widen at the sight. \"These must be a thousand years old, perhaps more! Yes, of course I'll take them.\"","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Demons"],"r":1}],[{"n":"The Sect member bolts out the door with an armful of produce. You're left with no other choice but to give chase into the New Market streets. He's no match for your speed, and in no time at all you've tackled him to the ground, spilling expensive produce everywhere. He thrashes against you, trying to snap his jaws onto your forearm. A quick blow to the forehead knocks him out cold, and the town guard arrives a few moments later.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}]],
    17: [[{"n":"As regulars transiting in and out of the city, you chat with the guards for a few minutes before they wave you and the crate through without inspection. An hour later, your silver-cloaked friend catches up to you further down the road.\n\n\"Well. Done? You have crate.\" The cloaked man smiles a disconcerting grin, cracking it open and handing you a pair of boots from the rows stowed inside. \"They will remember. Don't forget.\" You can't quite tell if it's a threat.","e":["Gain item 114 Gust Striders","Gain 1 reputation with Demons"]}],[{"n":"You give the guards a subtle look, tapping your thumb against the side of the crate. They catch on immediately, and, with some whispered instructions, wave you through.\n\nWhen the silver-cloaked man later catches up to you, the guards spring out of hiding, clasping him in irons. He snarls at you, spitting black ichor. \"Demons remember! Don't forget.\" The guards thank you for your help in getting this demon sympathizer off the streets, and are even kind enough to look away while you grab a set of contraband boots from inside the crate. It's a nice tip.","e":["Gain item 114 Gust Striders","Gain 1 reputation with Military","Lose 1 reputation with Demons"]}]],
    18: [[{"n":"It's evening before Nectar is outside her mother's manor and watchful eyes, browsing the markets in the Coin District. You approach her and are stopped by her handmaiden before you explain the situation. Nectar's eyes light up at the mention of Greggory, and she tears open the letter immediately. She reads through it twice before clutching it to her chest, tears of joy dotting her eyes. \"Yes, of course I'll marry him!\"","e":["Gain 15 collective gold","Scenario: start with Safeguard","Event card city 41"]}],[{"n":"You immediately hand the note over to his father, Councilman Greymare. \"It's good that you've brought this to me, I'll see to it that this foolishness is taken care of. He will understand and obey his father.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Gain 15 collective gold","Event card city 41"]}],[{"n":"You march the letter over to the Sekhem Gardens, where you find Councilwoman Vale entertaining a few Valraths over tea. She reviews the message then excuses herself to speak with you. \"That monstrous merchant and his family will never lay a finger on my daughters, mark my words. I absolutely forbid it! You have proven yourselves a valuable asset.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Gain 15 collective gold","Event card city 41"]}]],
    19: [[{"n":"The Merchant's Guild provides valuable services to these people, and everyone needs to pay their fair share. You step forward with the stern look your enemies learned too well, and after a moment of consternation, the grocer turns over a handful of coins to the tax collectors.\n\nThe collectors give you a nod, handing over a few coins for your assistance. \"It is unfortunate some merchants only respond to threats of violence. Truly a base outlook, but thank you for your efforts.\"","e":["Gain 5 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"],"r":1}],[{"t":["intimidating"],"c":"Trait: Intimidating","n":"You step up to show this group of shakedown artists just how little their \"protection\" really means. You grab the central collector by his collar and stare straight into his eyes. He stammers an apology and assures you the error must be in his ledger. \"I'll fix it—I'll fix it immediately.\" The stand operator looks delighted.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Scenario: start with Ward"],"r":1},{"o":1,"n":"You intercede on behalf of the grocer, and after some brief protests, the three tax collectors brush you off and head off to harass someone else. The grocer breathes a sigh of relief, thanking you for your help before turning back to selling his wares.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"],"r":1}]],
    20: [[{"n":"You shake the woman off and explain as best you can that you can't assist her right now. You make some vague promises about trying to find her later, but it's no use: soon the woman is bawling in the street, lamenting that no one will help her and how the rats will kill her in her sleep, then feast on her corpse. The whole speech is very graphic, and passersby begin to give you odd looks, wondering what you could have done to upset the poor woman so intensely.\n\nAt least you catch the merchant in time to collect your payment.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice.","Gain 20 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"You take pity on the poor woman and follow her back to her home, a ramshackle dwelling half-sunk into the muddy foundation. Sure enough, a family of three Vermlings has illegally moved into her cellar, living off her meager food supplies. You make a big show of reporting them to the guards and they begrudgingly pack their things to go. The old woman thanks you profusely and pays what she can.","e":["Each character gains 3 gold"]}]],
    21: [[{"c":"LOST ITEM COST > 25","n":"You cast your item as hard as you can into the Void. It tears your item to coarse black powder, producing a swirl of indigo light that catches your eye before vanishing. You feel a weight lifted and are excited for what the next year brings.","e":["Gain 2 battle goal checkmark(s)","Scenario: start with Ward"]},{"o":1,"n":"You toe just over the orange safety line and throw your item into the Void. As it disintegrates, it produces a lightshow that can't be seen anywhere else. You smile, excited for the coming year.","e":["Scenario: start with Ward"]}],[{"n":"You purchase a velvet dress from a vendor who assures you it belonged to a woman very dear to him. Sure enough, it produces a fantastic shower of sparks as the Void consumes it, and a cheer rises up from the crowd.","e":["Lose 15 collective gold","Each character gains 5 XP","Scenario: start with Bless"]}],[{"n":"You don't resonate with anything for sale, so you instead watch the offerings of others.","e":["Each character gains 2 XP"]}]],
    22: [[{"n":"The Jaws of the Lion are consummate professionals—your employer even sends a thank-you note for employing such sharply-dressed mercenaries (he particularly liked one of their fancy hats). They're the best of the best. Your employer even kicks in a hefty bonus, but there isn't much left after giving the Jaws their cut.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"c":"IF YOU HAVE \"Black Card\" 113","e":["Read section 72.4."]},{"o":1,"n":"You hear word the next day that the delivery was ambushed by thieves in transit. The Sin-Ra operated with ruthless efficiency, and while the robbers were killed, so were any witnesses, including the delivery driver. Your employer isn't pleased, but still pays for protecting the cargo. It's decent money, even after giving the Sin-Ra their cut.","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"n":"Boring security work doesn't need good manners. The delivery gets ambushed in transit by thieves, and the Four Crosses take a serious beating before being able to drive them off. Better them than you: it couldn't have happened to a more deserving group.","e":["Gain 25 collective gold"]}]],
    23: [[{"n":"In the man's clothes, you find a whopping forty gold, which you grab before the guards arrive. The next morning you're greeted at your door by the largest Savvas you've ever seen—a true walking mountain.\n\n\"You took Bonecruncher's money.\" The notorious loan shark known as \"Bonecruncher\" has made a name for himself around town, and you certainly don't want to be on his bad side. \"Don't worry, he doesn't want it back right now. Seems like he's taken an interest in you, so I'll be taking interest from you from now on.\" It turns to leave, ominously concluding with, \"see you soon.\"","e":["Gain 40 collective gold","Event card city 44","Gain trait: Indebted"]}],[{"rp":["military",2],"c":"Reputation with Military above 2","n":"The guards thank you for reporting it promptly, and after they take a statement, you're free to go. You hope they're able to find whoever did this and bring them to justice.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"Two days into the interrogation, the guards are even more convinced you're the killer. They even found blood on your boots, which you tried to explain was from an unrelated scenario. Eventually they release you with a court date. Hopefully you'll have better luck with the judges.","e":["Event card city 40"]}]],
    24: [[{"n":"He takes copious notes, but you come out of it feeling like you avoided any hot-button issues. Well, at least until you read the morning paper, which paints the Merchant's Guild in a miserable light. They're not pleased with the attention.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"n":"He takes copious notes, but you come out of it feeling like you avoided any hot-button issues. Well, at least until you read the morning paper, which paints the town guard in a miserable light. They're not pleased with the attention.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Lose 1 reputation with Military"]}],[{"n":"He takes copious notes, but you come out of it feeling like you avoided any hot-button issues. Well, at least until you read the morning paper, which paints the demons in an accurate but miserable light. They're not pleased with the attention.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Lose 1 reputation with Demons"]}],[{"n":"\"Some mercenaries. I guess if it doesn't involve cutting someone open, you're not interested, huh? Jerks.\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    25: [[{"c":"If you said Cade","n":"The Aesther in the unusual hat cracks a smile. \"Delightful, very good. Cade brought the green gift, loaded with not-quite-enough explosives. A costly mistake for what could've been a clean patricide.\"\n\nBonecruncher begins to stir. \"Is that true?\" Cade turns a shade of green that matches his gift, and Bonecruncher turns to you. \"We'll handle this within the family.\" In thanks, he hands you a mostly-not-burned gift, and that's the last you see of Cade.\n\nThe Aesther tips his hat. \"The name's Detective Elsewhere. Good to make your acquaintance!\" With that, he steps into a portal and is gone.","e":["Gain a random item design"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"No, I told you it was the green gift—a gift given by Cade, the middle child. Aerin is the eldest with the yellow gift, and Brint the youngest with red. Cade went to so much trouble loading that gift with explosives, he certainly deserves the credit for attempted patricide.\"\n\nBonecruncher begins to stir. \"Did you try to make this my last birthday?\" Cade turns a shade of green that matches his gift, and the muscle-bound Savvas bodyguard leads the family away.\n\nThe Aesther shrugs. \"Better luck next time, I suppose. Be seeing you.\" And with that, he steps into a portal and is gone.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]}]],
    26: [[{"rp":["military",8],"c":"Reputation with Military above 8","n":"You pull the guardsman aside and explain that interference with the mail system impacts everyone in the city. You vouch for this carrier and strongly recommend he lets her through, even without the required documentation. He sheepishly nods and waves her past.\n\n\"Finally! Now, where can I get a drink around here?\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]},{"o":1,"n":"You pull the new guardsman aside and attempt to explain he's giving the town guard a bad name. \"She's welcome to take it up with the council members. What's next? A warband claims they forgot their diplomatic sigil and I allow them to set up camp in the town square?\" You roll your eyes and leave them to work it out.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You keep the gathering crowd back and let the guard do his work. It takes nearly until dark, but he opens every package and records a complete manifest of the contents. Crude weapons, exotic pelts, and many, many satchels of assorted herbs.\n\n\"If she doesn't come up with the paperwork in forty eight hours, the entire lot will be impounded and put towards the city. I'm sure it won't come to that, though.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Gain 1 prosperity"]}]],
    27: [[{"rp":["merchant-guild",10],"c":"Reputation with Merchant Guild above 10","n":"His belongings turn out to be an odd mismatch of items: three new pairs of leather boots in different sizes, a set of copper mugs, an antique vase, and other sundry objects.\n\nThe shops are used to you dragging in piles of stuff from your adventures, and they don't bat an eye. You split the proceeds with him and he gives a gruff nod in thanks.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold","Tick a box"]},{"o":1,"n":"His belongings turn out to be an odd mismatch of items: three new pairs of leather boots in different sizes, a set of copper mugs, an antique vase, and other sundry objects.\n\nIt takes the better part of the afternoon to get everything sold, as many shopkeeps refuse to purchase what they perceive as stolen goods. By the time he takes his cut, there isn't much left.","e":["Gain 5 collective gold","Tick a box"]},{"c":"When all boxes are checked","e":["Read section 22.1.","Remove event card city 27"],"x":1}],[{"n":"You flag down the nearest guard. When you turn to point the man out, he's already fled. The guard confirms they've seen an uptick in criminals trying to find unsuspecting people to fence their goods for them. He thanks you for the report.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Tick a box"]},{"c":"When all boxes are checked","e":["Read section 93.2.","Remove event card city 27"],"x":1}]],
    28: [[{"e":["Read section 57.1."]}],[{"e":["Read section 77.5."]}]],
    29: [[{"c":"Pay 10 collective gold","n":"You drop a handful of coins into the gauntlet and the plink of metal against metal brings a smile to the guard's face. \"Thank you, friend! We'll see to it it's put to good use protecting fine citizens like you!\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity","Gain 1 reputation with Military"]},{"o":1,"e":["Apply outcome B"]}],[{"n":"You shake your head and walk past, and the guard quickly turns to other targets.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You take several minutes to deride the panhandling of the military, the effect on morale, and several exceptionally unkind things about the guards' presence in the city. You make clear in boisterous terms that the military presence begging for help from common citizens is a perfect metaphor for how they handle every problem, unable to do even something as simple as manage their own finances. The guard's friendly demeanor turns to absolute mortification by the time you wrap up ten minutes of dressing him down. A small group has gathered to watch the spectacle, and you finish with a few short words about why your preferred faction should be in charge.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Military","Gain 1 reputation with Merchants Guild or Sect."]}]],
    30: [[{"n":"The next morning, you make a full report to the watch captain, who in turn escalates it up the chain. The dirty looks of the two guards as they're forced to turn in their badges during the investigation is payment enough, but the appreciation of the higher-ups doesn't hurt, either.","e":["Gain 2 reputation with Military"]}],[{"t":["persuasive","intimidating"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive or Intimidating","n":"You agree to keep quiet on what you saw, but insist the guards put in a good word for you with the military brass. They're clearly appreciative of your good sense.\n\nYou do wonder what will happen to that Vermling, though.\n\nYou take a page out of the guards' book and demand they sweeten the deal for your silence.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Gain 10 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"You agree to keep quiet on what you saw, but insist the guards put in a good word for you with the military brass. They're clearly appreciative of your good sense.\n\nYou do wonder what will happen to that Vermling, though.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military"]}]],
    31: [[{"t":["aesther"],"c":"Trait: Aesther","n":"You grab the child and lift her clear of the haunting area. She is still screaming madly when the Aesther in your group lays a hand upon the child in deep concentration. Slowly, the crying subsides, and the child gets up and runs off.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice."]},{"o":1,"n":"You get the child off the sand as quickly as you can, but it doesn't do much good. The girl screams and screams, no matter what aid is administered, half of her face having taken on the sand-like texture of the Void itself. Eventually, a schoolteacher scoops her up and you continue on your way.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You watch to see what happens to the girl, making mental note for future reference. Her skin turns ashen and begins to flake away. She tries to stand, frantically brushing a thick black dust from her clothes as they fall away. Onlookers quickly rush to her aid, but it's clear half her body has been permanently scorched by the Void's corruption. You know some friends that would find this research helpful.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Demons"]}]],
    32: [[{"c":"If you said 3","n":"The old man opens his hand with a weary flair and a smile. \"Tell me, was it a lucky guess, or did you hear them? No one has heard them in a long while, since before Roland tore apart this city. Tell me you heard them! It's been so long!\""},{"n":"Choose one:"},{"e":["Tell him you heard them - Read section 15.5."]},{"e":["Tell him it was a random guess - Read section 40.5."]},{"o":1,"n":"The old man pops open his hand to show three gleaming glass beads. He snickers, as though it was a joke you should've seen coming. \"The voices really are gone.\" He looks despondent enough, you pick up his tab for the evening.","e":["Lose 5 collective gold"]}]],
    33: [[{"e":["When you have determined the face of the purse-snatcher, read section 81.3."]}]],
    34: [[{"n":"You proudly state you work with the Merchant's Guild, and would be happy to accept delivery.\n\nThe smile disappears from his face as he draws a thin blade from his package. In a flash and with expert precision, he thrusts it at you. He manages a few good hits before he runs off.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"n":"You politely explain that you're not in good favor with the Merchant's Guild, and wouldn't be able to direct him to anyone pertinent. The young man smiles a grin through a set of too-white teeth.\n\n\"Not a problem, I'll assure you you're better for it... I'm sure someone around here can accept delivery.\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    35: [[{"t":["outcast"],"c":"Trait: Outcast","e":["Apply outcome B"]},{"o":1,"n":"So as to not damage her confidence in her prosthetic, you reach out and touch her squishy, warm, left eye. You give it a couple of moist taps to confirm. A smile creeps across her face until she can't hold it in anymore.\n\n\"Hah! That's my real one!\" She pops out her glass eye, expertly rolling it across her knuckles—a feat even for someone sober, but she does it with practiced effortlessness. \"Best glass eye in Gloomhaven! You pop two of these in a Harrower, and it could pass for human, no question!\"","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]}],[{"t":["chaotic"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic","n":"There's only one way to get this right for certain. You extend two fingers and poke her in both eyes at once. \"Owww! What'd you do that for!?\" Some upset onlookers make clear you need to make it right, so you buy her a drink. It's enough to let everyone get on with the evening.","e":["Lose 2 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"It's pretty clear which eye is fake, and you're not one to take a dive on a direct challenge. You extend your finger and poke her right in the glass. \"Pfft. Lucky guess, that's all! I know you can't tell, no one can.\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    36: [[{"n":"You hand off the envelope to a hooded man in the Sinking Market. With a nod, he drops a sack of coins in your hand, and he doesn't seem in any rush as you take the time to count it. He thanks you for your help and says they'll call again if they need you in the future.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"You tear open the envelope and find detailed logs of guard movements throughout the Boiler District. The notes detail hours where security is lightest, and the shifts most likely to allow activities to go unnoticed. The records are weeks of work, and you can only imagine the value they'd have in the right hands. You could alert the guards or earn yourself a favor from a faction of your choosing.","e":["Gain either 2 reputation with the ruling faction or 1 reputation with any one other faction."]}]],
    37: [[{"n":"You visit Councilwoman Vale's office to plead for more funding. Her valet shoos you away with the assurance that it's a very important matter to the councilwoman, and you can be confident she'll look into it right away.","e":["Check one box below. If all boxes are checked, read section 131.2 and remove this card from the city deck.","Tick a box"]}],[{"n":"You ask how much it would take to accelerate the analysis. \"Oh, we need some additional radiance crystals, cabling certainly, and some additional protective equipment.\" A small fire starts at the back of the lab, and a Vermling casually dumps a pot of water on it—it's clear this isn't the first time.","e":["The party may lose 10 collective gold per box to check any number of boxes above in Outcome A. If all boxes in Outcome A are checked, read section 131.2 and remove this card from the city deck."]}]],
    38: [[{"n":"You swallow your pride and accept Bonecruncher's \"generous\" offer. If it really does get you off the hook for repayment, it's worth the time.","e":["Unlock scenario 95"]}],[{"t":["chaotic"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic","n":"You tear the newspaper out of the bodyguard's hands, shredding it with a scream. The Savvas guard looks surprised—even the dogs look confused, shying away behind the desk. You grab a half-finished drumstick off Bonecruncher's plate and lock gaze with him, biting it in half and swallowing, bone and all. A stillness falls across the room.\n\nJust when the silence becomes unbearable, Bonecruncher breaks out in a belly laugh. \"Hah, you're crazy! Anyone ever tell you that? I like crazy. Alright, I guess I can throw in a few coins for your effort. Don't let anybody ever tell you Bonecruncher isn't kind.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Unlock scenario 95"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to bargain for payment, but Bonecruncher rolls his eyes, and the bodyguard finally gets off its chair to escort you out. The massive Savvas isn't rough about it, but you can't help but feel it's just because it doesn't consider you a threat.","e":["Unlock scenario 95"]}]],
    39: [[{"n":"The drake follows you as you wind through the city, until you reach the central courtyard of the Traveler's District. While its initial approach left the populace terrified, its presence now commands a good deal of curiosity. You offhandedly note that the drake is seeking a meal.\n\nAn hour later, a queue has formed: quality vendors each waiting their turn to offer the drake a sample of their dishes. \"The seasoning is impeccable... mmmMm... is that arrowvine? And these tiny radishes!\" For weeks afterward, visitors come in the hopes of a repeat performance—one which you're thankful you don't need to orchestrate.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}],[{"n":"His torso blocks the entirety of the side-street, and only his head fits through the doorway, but the drake turns out to be a fun drinking companion. The bartender rolls out a fine barrel of juniper ale, and the meat pies are fresh this afternoon.\n\nHours later, the usual crowd is swapping stories with their newest, largest friend, who is responding with boisterous advice. \"No, you cannot be serious. He—hic!—did not say that to you. You could do so much better than him! Burn his house and move on, Janet.\" As the sun begins to crest the hilltops, the drake finally passes out, blocking the door. The patrons are happy to climb out the windows so as to not disturb him.","e":["Lose 10 collective gold","Gain 2 battle goal checkmark(s)"]}]],
    40: [[{"n":"You hire local counsel, a doting old Orchid who speaks with a slow drawl.","e":["REPUTATION WITH RULING FACTION > 15: Check box \"Prior Offense\" on the front of this event.; Lose 10 collective gold","Check box \"Prior Offense\" on the front of this event.; Lose 10 collective gold; Read section 120.2."]}],[{"t":["chaotic"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic","n":"You demand trial by combat, challenging the central arbiter. The bailiff is forced to restrain you.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with any faction of your choice."]},{"t":["persuasive","educated"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive or Educated","n":"You explain as best you can and throw yourself on the mercy of the court. They let you off with just a fine and a stern warning.","e":["Check box \"Prior Offense\" on the front of this event.","Lose 10 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"You use plenty of fancy-sounding words like \"criminal\" and \"accused\" and \"no guilt.\" You finish with a long, dramatic bow to allow for any applause, but silence hangs in the room.","e":["Check box \"Prior Offense\" on the front of this event.","Lose 10 collective gold","Read section 120.2."]}]],
    41: [[{"n":"The invitation looks to be in order, so you unclip the leather gate-rope and allow him to step aside. He scoffs a bit. \"I cannot fathom what took you so long. Perhaps literacy isn't a requirement for door-guards!\" He suddenly catches the eye of Councilman Greymare and instantly drops his indignation. \"Willem! It is a pleasure to see you!\" They disappear into the crowd.","e":["Draw event card city 42","Resolve event C-42 now."]}],[{"n":"You inform Basseloff that his invitation is counterfeit and that he will not be granted admittance. His eyes widen like two porcelain plates. \"WHAT DID YOU SAY TO I, BASSELOFF, THE GREATEST BARD THAT EVER LIVED?\"\n\nYou start to escort him from the premises when Councilwoman Vale rushes over. \"What is the meaning of this? Why have you laid hands on our esteemed guest?\" She is both trying to admonish you and pacify Basseloff, who appears on the verge of a stroke.\n\n\"THESE BRIGANDS REFUSED ME ENTRY! THESE—THESE TONE-DEAF CRITICS MUST BE EXPELLED IMMEDIATELY! I AM BASSELOFF!\"\n\nTen minutes later you're informed your services are no longer needed.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Military","Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}]],
    42: [[{"n":"You wave her through and can see the excitement on her face. An hour later, Councilwoman Vale and the wedding planner drag the young woman back to the entrance, fury in their eyes. \"Did you let this reporter through the door? Did you even look at her invitation? It's nonsense. It doesn't even have the groom's name spelled correctly!\" The young lady rushes down the stairs and out of sight. \"You're fired.\"","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Lose 1 reputation with Military"]}],[{"n":"You point out that the invitation is clearly a fake, and you refuse to let her through. She immediately drops the act, desperate.\n\n\"Please—I just want to see, to experience this. I spent a month's salary on this dress, I—I'm begging you, I won't say a word, no one will know I'm there.\" You look unmoved, and she scrambles around the interior of her purse. \"I have coin. I can make it worth your while. Please!\""},{"c":"Option A","e":["Accept a bribe to allow her entry.\nRead section 84.3."]},{"c":"Option B","e":["Refuse her entry. Read section 40.4."]}]],
    43: [[{"t":["hero"],"c":"Trait: Hero","n":"You recount, tastefully, just how incredible your performance was that day. The split-second that changed the fate of the nobleman's life, and your own, intertwining the two forevermore. You explain the fear, the momentary internal debate that gave way to your own grievous injury protecting another. You explain the hardship—again, tastefully—of your recovery, and in no time at all, people are buying you drinks. By the end of the evening, a pile of tips has built up in front of you.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Scenario: start with Bless","Each character without hero or friend-of-the-hero gains friend-of-the-hero."]},{"o":1,"n":"You relay the story you've heard a hundred times: the tale of your friend protecting a nobleman in complete disregard for their own safety. It's a good story, but it misses a bit of the punch by being told second-hand, and you can tell the crowd is just being polite by the end. A few folks are appreciative enough of the diversion to tip a few gold your way.","e":["Gain 5 collective gold"],"r":1}],[{"n":"\"Oh, sorry. Right, yeah... I thought you looked like someone who used to hang out with... never mind.\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    44: [[{"c":"No character has indebted","n":"\"Oh, our mistake. Enjoy your evening.\"","e":["No effect"]},{"c":"Each character has nimble","n":"You break out in a dead sprint, and the enforcers can't keep pace. You hear them shout after you: \"We'll catch up eventually!\"","e":["Add this card to the city deck as the fifth card from the top."]},{"o":1,"n":"It's a good fight, and by the time they finally tap, out everyone involved is bleeding, panting and sore. \"There'll always be more. You'll pay, you'll see.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Event card city 45"]}],[{"n":"\"Thank you for remaining in Bonecruncher's good graces, much obliged.\" The duo shake you down for what you're carrying, helping themselves to your savings. \"And it's always nice to keep track of who's good for a debt.\"","e":["Each character loses half of their gold (rounded up). Each character without indebted gains indebted."]}]],
    45: [[{"rp":["military",15],"c":"Reputation with Military above 15","n":"You flag down a passing guard, who promises to look into the matter. A few days later, at the barracks, you're told the investigation has determined it was a passing Vermling thief—they've already caught him, he confessed, and he's been sentenced to six months in the Ghost Fortress. You try to explain it wasn't a Vermling, but a Savvas, and the guard looks away, suddenly nervous. \"It's above my pay grade. We did recover some of the funds, hopefully that helps put this matter behind us.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Add this card to the city deck as the fifth card from the top."]},{"o":1,"n":"You flag down a passing guard, who promises to look into the matter. Checking in at the Barracks a few days later, you find the report was conveniently misplaced. \"You said it was related to a missed payment to Bonecruncher? Sometimes these things happen... you should pay off that debt, if you know what's good for you.\"","e":["Add this card to the city deck as the fifth card from the top."]}],[{"n":"After a few hours effort, some very long nails, and heavy planks of oak, you've rebuilt your door stronger than it was before—let's see anyone try to break through that!","e":["No effect"]}]],
    46: [[{"n":"Apollon's arm may be broken, but he's a trained fighter and can still pose as a challenging sparring partner. He shows you some moves he's perfected in the field and you spend a few hours swapping combat stories.\n\nBefore he departs for the night, he explains the mission: \"It's been too long since the Green Carapace has been sighted, and rumors of its demise are spreading. The Sin-Ra are producing some sort of poison serum in a warehouse by the docks—I need you to make a mess of their operation and pose as the vigilante while you do it. Keep fear going in the hearts of evil... it would be unfortunate for my progress to backslide.\"","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Each character gains a perk mark.","Gain trait: Carapace Combatant","Unlock scenario 91"]}],[{"n":"\"Then I'll pay for two jobs: rescuing the distressed, and sealing your lips.\" He hands over a mountain of coins.\n\nBefore he departs for the night, he explains the mission: \"It's been too long since the Green Carapace has been sighted, and rumors of its demise are spreading. The Sin-Ra are producing some sort of poison serum in a warehouse by the docks—I need you to make a mess of their operation and pose as the vigilante while you do it. Keep fear going in the hearts of evil... it would be unfortunate for my progress to backslide.\"","e":["Gain 50 collective gold","Unlock scenario 91"]}]],
    47: [[{"n":"A member of the medical team patches you up outside, tending to your wounds. First Shield Harmon slaps you on the back, prompting a coughing fit. \"Unfortunate you picked an explosive crate instead of the stolen gold. Odds were just against us. We'll get those thieving bastards someday, though, you'll see.\"","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"A guard finishes brushing the soot off your back, engrossed in your story. \"Really impressive, you only had a twenty five percent chance of finding it under those conditions.\"\n\nAnother guard chimes in: \"It would've been fifty percent, wouldn't it?\"\n\nThe first guard shakes his head. \"No, hang on—would it have been seventy five percent?\"\n\nYou leave them to argue and hand the recovered gold over to First Shield Harmon, who is uncharacteristically smiling.\n\n\"Let's make a deal: I'll give you a cut of your findings for your help, and you get some well-earned rest.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Gain 20 collective gold"]}]],
    48: [[{"t":["vermling"],"c":"Trait: Vermling","n":"You arrange to have some Vermlings stop by and they quickly drag the body out the back door and down into the sewers—you suspect it won't resurface.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold"]},{"rp":["military",12],"c":"Reputation with Military above 12","n":"You flag down a passing guard patrol and they complacently nod along. The whole matter is very discrete and done before daybreak.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold"]},{"rp":["demons",12],"c":"Reputation with Demons above 12","n":"You produce a small urn of powder, tracing it around the body. With the strike of a match, a full-sized flame demon appears and incinerates the corpse.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"It just takes a bit of gold to keep people's mouths shut and get the corpse out.","e":["Gain 5 collective gold"]}],[{"t":["strong","resourceful"],"c":"Trait: Strong or Resourceful","n":"You roll the corpse up in the rug to move it. Gloomhaven has enough unmonitored alleyways that it'll be a long time before it's discovered.","e":["Read section 101.5."]},{"o":1,"n":"The nobleman looks concerned as you have trouble hefting the corpse out the door.","e":["Read section 93.1."]}]],
    49: [[{"n":"You step forward with the stern look your enemies learned too well, and after a moment of consternation the grocer turns over a handful of coins to the tax collectors.\n\nThe collectors give you a delighted nod, handing over a few coins for your assistance. \"I'll remind them just how helpful you were as soon as I return to the office!\" The collectors quickly make their way off to other business.","e":["Each character gains 5 gold"]}],[{"n":"You look up and down the \"tax collector\" before you and notice the minor inconsistencies—a brass pin rather than bronze, and an ill-fitting suit on what should be a sharply-dressed collector. It's an excellent dupe, but these are some clever con men trying to pick up coin for themselves. When confronted, they quickly drop the act. \"We, the uh—the Merchant's Guild, that is, because I speak for the Merchant's Guild, the uh—taxes are free today, thank you!\" The kids bolt.\n\nThe grocer's eyes widen, and he passes off some delicious fruit as thanks.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}]],
    50: [[{"n":"You let him know the price and he drops the coins on the counter, grabbing the axe before you've even had a chance to count it. \"I guess you were too busy sweeping the shop to bother buying this beauty. Well, good luck finding work—I'm sure things'll turn around for mercenaries as good as you are!\" He holds back a laugh as the group departs. A few hours later, the shopkeep returns, relieved you're still there. He offers you a discount on anything in the store.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Each character may immediately purchase one item from the available item supply for half price."]}],[{"n":"You tell him it's double the actual price. \"That's... basically everything I have.\" He looks a bit sheepish. \"Whatever, I still want it.\" He drops the 40 gold on the counter and turns to leave. \"Good luck staying open with prices like these. You're lucky I'm super rich and can afford it!\" He intentionally bumps a display of pole arms to the ground on his way out, eliciting laughs from his friends. A few hours later, the shopkeep returns and offers you a discount on his wares. You don't mention your \"enhanced\" pricing.","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Each character may immediately purchase one item from the available item supply for half price."]}]],
    51: [[{"n":"\"Okay, yeah, okay,\" the guard nods, finally accepting the inevitable. You tell him it's not so bad being a part of something bigger than himself, and the Orchid bruisers slowly release him from the wall. As soon as his feet touch the ground, though, the soldier tries to make a run for it—but skewers himself on an Orchid's outstretched dagger.\n\n\"What a waste,\" the Sect enforcer says to you as the young soldier slumps to the ground. \"Thanks for trying, anyway.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Demons"]}],[{"rp":["demons",5],"c":"Reputation with Demons above 5","n":"You tell the Sect enforcers that their faith must be weak if they believe the city's coming salvation could be brought down by one kid. They grumble and back down, letting the guard escape with his life.","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"o":1,"n":"The Sect enforcers drop the soldier and turn their attention to you. The fight is short; your opponents are strong, but they're common back-alley brawlers—you kill monsters for a living.","e":["Each character gains 5 XP","Lose 1 reputation with Demons"],"r":1}]],
    52: [[{"n":"You climb to the bottom of a sinkhole, where you discover a wide, freshly-dug tunnel. You follow it to the end, where you find a group of earth demons digging toward the West Barracks. They turn and charge, and you're forced to kill them before they grind you into the tunnel floor.","e":["Scenario: suffer 2 damage","Lose 1 reputation with Demons"]}],[{"t":["strong"],"c":"Trait: Strong","n":"\"Can't pay\" is your least favorite trait in a potential client. The guards are paid to protect the city-let them handle it. You approach the officer in charge of the military presence in the Sinking Market.\n\nThe officer groans dramatically. \"I can't,\" he whines, \"but you look like a hearty bunch. Can I just pay you to handle this?\"","e":["Each character gains 3 gold","Apply outcome A"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"Can't pay\" is your least favorite trait in a potential client. The guards are paid to protect the city-let them handle it. You approach the officer in charge of the military presence in the Sinking Market.\n\nThe officer puts up a fuss, but eventually admits that yes, it is his job to investigate. He dispatches a small crew of soldiers, who return with reports that the sinkholes were caused by earth demons digging a tunnel toward the West Barracks. You don't get paid, but at least you didn't have to get your hands dirty.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    53: [[{"n":"You rush to the city walls and see an Inox warband mounted atop sturdy garralevs ready to breach the Northern Gate. Only twenty guards were left behind while the others train. They range from expert marksmen to those too infirm to join the field exercises.\n\n\"True Shields!\" an exhausted runner sputters out. \"We spotted a smaller force massing outside the Western Gate—it may be a surprise attack!\" You'll need to divide the forces to defend the city.","e":["Read section 5.1."]}],[{"n":"You've done more than your share of defending Gloomhaven already. You head to the Sleeping Lion, content to let the professionals handle it. It takes a week to clean up after the attack breaches the walls, but at least you're not nursing wounds.","e":["Until the next scenario is completed, no character may buy or sell any item, enhance a card, or retire."]}]],
    54: [[{"rp":["merchant-guild",13],"c":"Reputation with Merchant Guild above 13","n":"You head to the Coin District and meet with a member of the Merchant's Guild you've had dealings with before. He looks at you skeptically, but says he will see what he can do about making the area more livable.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]},{"o":1,"n":"Every merchant you try to talk to about the issue laughs you out of the room. Why help others when there is no profit in it for them?","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"c":"Pay 25 collective gold","n":"You can't do much politically for the boy, but you have the funds to bankroll him yourself. You put him and his mother up in better housing in the Boiler's District. It's not as safe as you'd like, but at least he won't have to deal with flooding anymore. Maybe these little acts can make a difference.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity","Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"o":1,"n":"You can't bankroll his life, but you do what you can to help him out of the rut he's in. While he hoped for more, he thanks you for the help you provide.","e":["Lose 5 collective gold"]}]],
    55: [[{"c":"Lose 20 Collective Gold (Or 10 gold if persuasive or Military reputation > 9)","n":"You offer to pay your fines right now, without involving that messy judicial system. The guards agree and quickly pocket the money.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"e":["Apply outcome C"]}],[{"n":"You turn yourself in to the mercy of the guards. It takes several days locked up in the Ghost Fortress before your case is heard, and even then, it takes everything you have to convince the council members reviewing your file that there isn't sufficient evidence to convict you. By the time you're released a week later, the guards are having a good chuckle. Seems they've \"misplaced\" some of your coinage.","e":["Each character loses half their gold."]}],[{"n":"You shove the foremost guard to the ground and take off sprinting. You're able to lose them in the crowded streets, for now.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Military","Place this card back on top of the city deck.","Trait: Nimble or Intimidating: Place it one card deeper for each instance of either trait you have."],"r":1}]],
    56: [[{"n":"\"Do not lament your position, for you are playing your role, just as the Guild does. Power is a fearful place, as it must protect itself, lest it lose all it has. Your existence challenges power, and balance must be restored.\"\n\nThe fight lasts just a few seconds, but it feels like fending off an army's worth of attacks, dagger strikes slashing you repeatedly. With a crackle of final energy, the alleyway goes quiet. You hear a voice reverberate from the rooftops: \"The Guild fears that which it cannot control. Until you meet my blades again...\"","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Scenario: start with Wound","Scenario: suffer 3 damage","Discard 1"]}],[{"rp":["merchant-guild",2],"c":"Reputation with Merchant Guild above 2","n":"You shout something about his contract being outdated, and he gives pause, looking down at the device on his wrist. \"My apologies. Time is difficult for me to track, and I fear you are correct: my endeavor is past necessity. It serves no purpose to murder you today. An example need not be made.\"","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You offer to pay off your own bounty to avoid the fight. \"Power can be fear, flesh, or funds. Can you afford the price to restore balance?\"","e":["You may pay 5 collective gold per reputation with the Merchants Guild below 3 you have.","Apply outcome A"]}]],
    57: [[{"n":"You walk up to their table with a disarming smile, then kick the table into the stomach of the man on the far side. In no uncertain terms, you describe how this bar helped put the very leadership they're plotting against into power, and you'll stop at nothing to protect it. The dissidents cast terrified looks amongst themselves, bolting for the exit at the first sign you'll let them leave without a beating.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with the ruling faction."]}],[{"n":"You order a round of juniper ale and hand-deliver it to their table. They're instantly suspicious, but after a few hours of talking (and a few more rounds on your tab), they give each other careful looks and test the waters:\n\n\"We're assembling a team of people... people interested in taking back power for the citizens of Gloomhaven. There's a man named Loop, he's been organizing a resistance—I think he'd like to meet you. You seem like good people, the kind of people Gloomhaven was founded by. Will you join us?\"\n\nYou nod, and plans begin in earnest.\n\n\"The silent will have a voice.\"","e":["Event card city 58"]}]],
    58: [[{"n":"The first strike is waved off as an inconvenience, but as the coordinated explosions begin to rock government buildings, word spreads quickly: Gloomhaven is not safe for those in power, and the citizenry have the rudder to steer the course of their lives. You can see it on faces in the town square—there is hope. There is something for the government to fear.","e":["Lose 2 reputation with the ruling faction. Gain 1 reputation with each other faction.","Event card city 59"]}],[{"n":"You head out from the meeting and go immediately to your contacts in Gloomhaven's ruling class. With the information you gathered, it's a simple matter to round up the dissidents from their beds before the morning strike, allowing the citizenry to sleep soundly for another day, none the wiser of the threat to the safety of the city. The silent have been silenced.","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Gain 2 reputation with the ruling faction."]}]],
    59: [[{"n":"\"Wisdom to ask for compensation up front—no one knows what tomorrow brings but change.\" He draws a series of marks on the map of the Silent Bridge, detailing its weak points. \"The foundation of the bridge predates Gloomhaven's recent founding. It was built with the old ways, in the old fashion of permanence. We will bring it down with the power of chaos.\" His eyes flicker deep black, and he opens his palm to reveal a swirl of azure energy.\n\n\"They won't know what hit them.\"","e":["Gain 30 collective gold","Unlock scenario 100"]}],[{"n":"\"Grace is not limited to the nobility, thank you. I assure you the resources will be put to nothing but the improvement of our home.\" He draws a series of marks on the map of the Silent Bridge, detailing its weak points. \"The foundation of the bridge predates Gloomhaven's recent founding. It was built with the old ways, in the old fashion of permanence. We will bring it down with the power of chaos.\" His eyes flicker deep black, and he opens his palm to reveal a swirl of azure energy.\n\n\"They won't know what hit them.\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity","Unlock scenario 100"]}]],
    60: [[{"n":"Loop's gold eyes flash, leaving him with a bit of a smirk. \"If I didn't know the good those hands have produced, I would take you for a scoundrel. But I know you will put coin to trouble wherever you go. Take it, and may you further give voice to those who cannot speak.\"","e":["Gain 20 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"With strained movement, he rises from his seat, dumping a purse of coins across the table. He speaks loudly, drawing the attention of others across the basement. \"You heard these mercenaries—even when offered to line their own pockets, they seek to lift us all.\" He invites his followers to the table. \"Take this, and spread it where needed. Let us be a force for the commoner where Gloomhaven's leadership has failed.\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}]],
    61: [[{"n":"You rip open the package and find a logbook. The pages detail eight young interns working for Councilman Myte, each of which never made it to their two-month review. Clear records detail dates and times for payments, but the ledger shows the final payments were never made. You stow the book in your satchel and consider the best time to use this information.","e":["Gain trait: Blackmailer","Event card city 62","Event card city 63"]}],[{"n":"If someone wants to use your services, you want to know why. He has a head start, but you close the gap to the hooded figure. You grasp at his cloak and attempt to tackle him to the ground, but he deftly twists and rolls, leaving you holding nothing but fabric. Whoever this is, they're well-trained. He smashes a vial of something into the wall beside you and a choking gas leaves you panting. When it clears, he's gone.\n\nWaiting to regain your breath, you tear open the package he left. Inside is a logbook of records which details Councilman Myte hiring interns, then their subsequent disappearance just before they reach their third month of employment. Curious.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle","Gain trait: Blackmailer","Event card city 62","Event card city 63"]}]],
    62: [[{"n":"\"This is the original, but if you have made any copies, I will assure you it is the last mistake of your lives. You will find me a pugnacious adversary.\" He opens a desk drawer and aggressively tosses a coin purse towards you. You take the time to count it, slowly. When all is confirmed, he snatches the logbook and casts it immediately into the fire. \"Now get out of my sight!\"","e":["Gain 30 collective gold","Lose trait: Blackmailer","Remove event card city 63"]}],[{"n":"\"Yes, fine. Fine! I will see to it that your requests are effected. Now, the book—and this had best be the only copy, or you will find my reach, and my anger, knows no bounds.\" He snatches the logbook and casts it immediately into the fire. \"Now get out of here.\"","e":["Gain 2 reputation with any one faction of your choice.","Lose trait: Blackmailer","Remove event card city 63"]}],[{"n":"A week later, you return to your lodging to find the room has been overturned—your belongings are scattered everywhere, and a sticky black sludge has been poured over your bedsheets. There's nothing to confirm who you owe the visit to, but you have a decent hunch. Still worth it.","e":["Lose 10 collective gold"]}]],
    63: [[{"n":"You open the paper the next day to read the explosive piece about Councilman Myte, but can't find it anywhere. You do find an obituary mourning the loss of a young reporter found dead in her apartment, though.","e":["Gain 25 collective gold","Lose trait: Blackmailer","Remove event card city 62"]}],[{"n":"You brush the young woman off, refusing to give up your intel in pursuit of some splashy story. You'll find justice for those interns your own way.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    64: [[{"n":"\"If my source is correct—and they'd better be, for what I paid—there's an unmarked graveyard not far from here, in the Corpsewood. Councilman Myte makes a trip that direction every other month, which coincides directly with when he gets a new intern... and his old one goes missing. The last one was a young woman, excited for the opportunity to work for a council member. Her mother said she wore a necklace with a feather on it.\"\n\nYour old friend looks away for a moment, then steels their resolve. \"It's distasteful, but I need you to find her.\" The council member grits their teeth. \"Bring a shovel.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 81"]}],[{"n":"\"Right, of course. I wouldn't dream of sending you off without an advance.\" You're not totally convinced the newly minted politician wasn't angling for a favor. \"If my source is correct—and they'd better be, for what I paid—there's an unmarked graveyard not far from here, in the Corpsewood. Councilman Myte makes the trip that direction every other month, which coincides directly with when he gets a new intern... and his old one goes missing. The last one was a young woman, excited for the opportunity to work for a council member. Her mother said she wore a necklace with a feather on it.\"\n\nYour old friend looks away for a moment, then steels their resolve. \"It's distasteful, but I need you to find her.\" The council member grits their teeth. \"Bring a shovel.\"","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Unlock scenario 81"]}]],
    65: [[{"n":"You give a list of grievances. Your old mercenary friend takes copious notes, and it seems like they sincerely want to help. \"Thank you—that grounded perspective is what I've been missing. I'll do everything I can to help.\"\n\nWhen you finally part ways, you can't help feeling like you encountered a celebrity—one that can actually make a difference.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}],[{"n":"You explain that the taxation of the merchants has prevented them from making enough profit to bring new goods into town, and everything for sale has grown stale. The council member takes copious notes, and it seems like they sincerely want to help. \"Thank you—that grounded perspective is what I've been missing. I'll do everything I can to help.\"\n\nWhen you finally part ways, you can't help feeling like you encountered a celebrity—one that can actually make a difference. You've just started on your journey when a mousy council aide catches up to you, panting. \"Excuse me! The council member asked that I get this your way immediately!\" It's a wrapped box with a note from your old friend.\n\nIt reads: \"Let's each make Gloomhaven better our own way.\"","e":["Gain a random item design"]}]],
    66: [[{"t":["immunity"],"c":"Trait: Immunity","n":"You ward everyone away while you load the bodies onto a cart, take them outside the city, and burn them. You return to a group of guards who don't appreciate disposing of dead bodies before they can investigate them.\n\nYou wash and manage to pass for clean. Well, at least as clean as normal.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Military"]},{"o":1,"n":"You ward everyone away while you load the bodies onto a cart, take them outside the city, and burn them. You return to a group of guards who don't appreciate disposing of dead bodies before they can investigate them.\n\nHours later, you find an odd growth on your arm. Lancing the pustule produces a murky liquid that reeks of sewage. It passes, but not soon enough.","e":["Scenario: start with Poison","Lose 1 reputation with Military"]}],[{"t":["herald of xorn"],"c":"Trait: Herald Of Xorn","n":"You approach the corpses with morbid fascination. The number of insects is alarming, as are the diseased sores.\n\nYou call out an invitation to the skittering creatures covering the corpses. The assembled crowd watches in horror as they skitter up your cloak and into your being. Consumption never felt so good.","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"o":1,"n":"You approach the corpses with morbid fascination. The number of insects is alarming, as are the diseased sores.\n\nThe disease spreads throughout the Sinking Market, killing many more people. Supplies grow scarce.","e":["Until you successfully complete a scenario, the cost of purchasing all items is increased by 5 gold."]}]],
    67: [[{"n":"\"Oh, so it's a rescue op?\" The Vermling swivels around in her chair. \"Probably want the mission room, then.\" She pulls a lever under the reception desk, and the wall to your right slides open, revealing a veritable armory of weapons and equipment hidden behind an ordinary-looking wall. \"Boss is a little... cautious. Still keeps some weird hobbies. Guess you can't take the mercenary out of a person, really.\"\n\nAcross the wall is a blueprint for something you haven't seen before. The Vermling concierge sees your interest. \"Boss was working on that, says it'll be pretty great when it's finished. You're welcome to it if you think it'll help. Just bring Boss back safely, yeah?\"","e":["Gain a random item design","Unlock scenario 85"]}],[{"n":"You thank the Vermling concierge for her time and avoid hinting that anything is amiss. \"Thanks for stopping in. I'll let Boss know you stopped by.\"\n\nIf your old friend needs help, you'll answer the call.","e":["Unlock scenario 85"]}]],
    68: [[{"n":"The Wayward Inn, owned by none other than the Greymare family, isn't hard to find, even for someone who hasn't visited Gloomhaven before. It's the most prominent structure in the Traveler's District, with a purple roof that crests high over other buildings to ensure a guest's view by a wide margin. You direct the old man northward and he gives a thankful sigh of relief, handing over a few coins for the trouble.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"It's an opportunity to support your friend's new business, so you'll take time out of your day to help make a sale. You walk the gentleman over to your old adventuring partner's inn, assuring him it'll be a much better—and more cost effective—alternative for him and his guests.\n\n\"Thank you, truly. I've seen so many neer-do-wells in my time, I felt I was surely going to be accosted any moment. I appreciate the kindness—and you said you knew the proprietor of this establishment? They're trustworthy? I have a delegation of twelve coming in from Keyport, so we'll need a number of rooms...\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}]],
    69: [[{"n":"You invite the Sin-Ra Syndicate member outside for a more clandestine discussion. As soon as you've stepped into the alley, you spring the attack, ending him quickly. You find a note with instructions laying out your worst fears:\n\n\"Traitor has been traced to the Sleeping Lion. Likely posing as a mercenary to avoid detection. Find and execute. The Sin-Ra leaves no survivors.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"You look to the other members of your party, drawing the Black Card out and setting it on the table. For such a simple object, it feels so very heavy. There is a moment of calm before the Valrath lunges at you with his dagger.\n\nThe technique is familiar, though, and the ambush unsurprising. You deflect and smash his head against the tabletop. With a hiss he tries to grasp at you, but a kick under the table sends him backwards into a passing patron. Never the locale to turn down a bar fight, the Sleeping Lion erupts into chaos, and in the ensuing commotion, your Valrath attacker conveniently finds a dagger in his belly. There won't be anyone to report back to his masters in the Sin-Ra, but the cover is clumsy, and word will still travel. You'll need to go deeper underground.","e":["Increase the number of side scenarios you need to complete for your personal quest to 7 (note it on your character sheet)."]}]],
    70: [[{"n":"You deftly steer the conversation to other topics, including any aspects of matters outside the city. Some loose lips give a great lead, and you slip back out with the Sin-Ra none the wiser.","e":["Unlock a random side scenario."]}],[{"t":["persuasive"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive","n":"You share that you heard the imposter was a red-headed brawler with a mohawk, and everyone agrees to keep an eye out for them. That should keep them nicely off your trail.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]},{"o":1,"n":"You try to explain that you heard the imposter was traveling with a group of mercenaries, mercenaries that look very unlike the ones you're here with tonight. The explanation results in some raised eyebrows, and you make your way out of the meeting shortly thereafter.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    71: [[{"n":"\"The Sin-Ra works as a series of sleeper cells, each isolated from the others. It's how this Black Card let me access so many places—each unit is blind to the workings of the others. But even a network as dispersed as this requires leadership... and that is the Grand Vizier. This very night, he will arrive from White Oak, and I will end his life. It is our last chance.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 82"]}],[{"n":"You agree to help your old friend, setting a time to meet later that night. You let them get well out of sight, then take the opportunity to knock on the door of the secret hideout and alert them. A few words is all it takes to give them warning of the impending attack.\n\nThe next morning, a beggar woman shows up at your door. She wordlessly licks her lips and sets a heavy bag of coin in your palm. You can't help but notice the pouch is stained with blood.","e":["Gain 30 collective gold"]}]],
    72: [[{"n":"You thank the actuary for bringing you such good fortune. It's not often that losing a friend is so lucrative. \"Be well, and please keep my card. I also offer exemplary mortician services.\" He tips his hat and leaves you to count your prize.","e":["Gain 50 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"He packs his paperwork into a leather briefcase. \"Yes, well, I understand the subject matter may be distasteful. You are not the first next-of-kin to refuse, of course. In such instances, I will see to it that the funds are put towards the common good.\" He stands, tipping his hat. \"Good day to you, and my apologies for the intrusion.\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}],[{"n":"\"You want to set up a tontine between just the people at this table? I would be honored to assist. Here are the funds you've earned, and I'll draw up the new paperwork.\"","e":["Gain 50 collective gold","Collectively choose an amount of gold. Each character that wants to participate in the tontine pays that amount. Mark your participation and total amount paid on your character sheet. When all other participating characters have retired, the last remaining participating character receives the combined total of gold paid by all participating characters."]}]],
    73: [[{"t":["chaotic","strong"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic or Strong","n":"You break a chair over a man's back, kick him in the teeth, and then you really get into it. It's a bar brawl that could only be described as \"epic\".","e":["Each character gains 5 XP"]},{"o":1,"n":"You jump into the melee, breaking heads and chairs in equal measure. You've seen worse brawls, but the proprietor still isn't happy when the dust settles.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"t":["nimble"],"c":"Trait: Nimble","n":"You selectively acquire a handful of coins from some unsuspecting or unconscious people. Even after tipping the proprietor, it was a fruitful night.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"You try to snatch a coin purse off a drunk merchant, but he grabs your arm.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Apply outcome A"]}],[{"t":["chaotic"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic","n":"You start to calm the patrons, but one clocks you in the jaw. Oh well, you gave peace a chance.","e":["Apply outcome A"]},{"o":1,"n":"You manage to calm down the Inox and buy off the rest of the room with some extra drinks. The proprietor breathes a sigh of relief.","e":["Lose 5 collective gold"]}]],
    74: [[{"n":"He snaps the thin string on his cobble, and the memory crystals roll across the table. He scoops them up gently, sorting them into each of your hands."},{"c":"If you indivdially selected A","e":["Scenario: start with Bless:2"]},{"c":"If you individually selected B","e":["Gain trait: Memory Of Serenity"]},{"n":"\"Hope they're worth as much to you as the next round is to me.\"","e":["Lose 3 collective gold","Event card road 41"]}]],
    75: [[{"n":"You pull back the canvas sheet and notch an arrow—you draw the bow, hold your breath steady, and let loose. The arrow sails through four axes before ricocheting to the ground. Not bad, and the practice gives you a good idea of what to expect tomorrow.","e":["Read section 36.3 and you succeed on one axe head you'd otherwise fail."]}],[{"n":"You hurry to bed and get a good night's sleep, dreaming of a clean shot through the axe heads. You wake up refreshed and ready to win this competition.","e":["Read section 36.3 and gain advantage on your first draw."]}],[{"n":"Given the precision with which these axes have been installed in the stage, it's a small matter to nudge a few out of position. No one will be able to land a clean shot tomorrow.","e":["Read section 89.3."]}]],
    76: [[{"t":["harrower"],"c":"Trait: Harrower","e":["Apply outcome C"]},{"o":1,"n":"If they've come all this way, it's likely for something uncommon to them but common to you—to the Sinking Market it is. After wandering the stalls for nearly an hour, they spot it: powdered axenuts! They give you a tip for the trouble, and you're happy to move on.","e":["Gain 5 collective gold"]}],[{"t":["harrower"],"c":"Trait: Harrower","e":["Apply outcome C"]},{"o":1,"n":"If there's a place that would have the unique fare they're looking for, it's the exotic offerings of the New Market. Unfortunately, after great effort and a lot of dirty looks, you can't locate the spice they're looking for, and the sight of the Harrowers is driving off legitimate business. Everyone is happy when you direct them to the Sinking Market, and the Harrowers tip you for the trouble.","e":["Gain 5 collective gold","Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"n":"If they've come all this way, it's likely for something uncommon to them but common to you—to the Sinking Market it is. You share a portion of your bugs and commune consciousnesses. With a direct line into their mind, you quickly determine the spice they're looking for is a powdered form of axenuts: simple to find, and a healthy tip for you.","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Gain 1 prosperity"]}]],
    77: [[{"n":"You open the crate and release it just outside the home. You can't help but notice several of the bugs crawling right back inside. No harm in repeat business.","e":["Each character gains 2 gold"],"r":1}],[{"t":["persuasive"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive","n":"You walk into the Brown Door, a seedy dive bar in the Old Docks. Your \"Harrower\" friend generously orders several rounds for everyone present—it's a phenomenal evening. The last time you see the crate full of bugs, it's being hit on by a very tipsy woman.","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"o":1,"n":"After a few minutes of unconvincing excuses, you're forced to pay your tab and are thrown out. You leave the crate in the street and wander on your way.","e":["Lose 2 collective gold"]}],[{"t":["harrower","vermling"],"c":"Trait: Harrower or Vermling","n":"You select the best of the crate's offerings for consumption. Juicy, fat insects are the perfect way to bulk up. Delicious!","e":["Each character gains 2 gold","Each character gains 5 XP"]},{"o":1,"n":"The crunch of exoskeleton is deeply unsettling. It's made worse as you suddenly remember the dusty, dirty state of the home you just drove these out of. Disgusting.","e":["Each character gains 2 gold","Scenario: start with Poison"]}]],
    78: [[{"c":"Average character level > 3","n":"You spend the afternoon reviewing the city's defense plans, ultimately putting together a new training regimen. The guards go home that night exhausted from the additional drills, but the leadership is very pleased with your contribution.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Military"]},{"o":1,"n":"You spend the day training the new recruits. By the time the sun goes down, their skills are much improved, and they're grateful to you for the help.","e":["Gain 5 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Military"]}],[{"n":"The Merchant's Guild is eager to hear about the problem spots of the city guard. \"Politically, this is valuable. There is also the matter of evading some of the more cumbersome taxes... Thank you for bringing this to us.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"n":"You secretly contact a known member of the Sect and provide the information. He listens intently, finally turning over a handful of coins in thanks. \"We will use this well, siblings.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Demons"]}]],
    79: [[{"n":"The lead scientist steps up as close to the Void as good sense dictates, visibly nervous. Two Orchids step beside him and link hands, emitting a high-pitched tone that channels the arcane energies. After a few moments, they seem to settle on an appropriate frequency, at which time a Savvas joins their midst, carrying the sacred branch. With the ritualistic setup complete, a swirl of white light emerges from the Savvas' chest, encircling the group. The Orchids' harmony reaches an ear-piercing crescendo, and the bough of the Sacred Oak tree lifts of its own accord out of the Savvas' hands into the air. It is suspended for just a moment before it fires with impossible speed into the swirling blackness of the Void, disintegrating on contact as all things do.\n\n\"We have the results! To my impossible surprise, the Void and the Great Oak are exactly the same age!\" The crowd gasps. \"More research will be required!\"\n\nThe man beside you shrugs. \"Meh, just happy I don't owe you 15 gold.\"","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"The lead scientist steps up as close to the Void as good sense dictates, visibly nervous. Two Orchids step beside him and link hands, emitting a high-pitched tone that channels the arcane energies. After a few moments, they seem to settle on an appropriate frequency, at which time a Savvas joins their midst, carrying the sacred branch. With the ritualistic setup complete, a swirl of white light emerges from the Savvas' chest, encircling the group. The Orchids' harmony reaches an ear-piercing crescendo, and the bough of the Sacred Oak tree lifts of its own accord out of the Savvas' hands into the air. It is suspended for just a moment before it fires with impossible speed into the swirling blackness of the Void, disintegrating on contact as all things do.\n\n\"We have the results! To my impossible surprise, the Void and the Great Oak are exactly the same age!\" The crowd gasps. \"More research will be required!\"\n\nThe man beside you shrugs. \"Well, I suppose I lost, since it isn't technically older. I thought the Oak was the oldest thing there is. Fine, take your money.\"","e":["Gain 15 collective gold"]}]],
    80: [[{"n":"The class runs until well past dark. While you're left sore from the spartan wooden seating, your mind is racing with the techniques, methods, and tactics the lecturers presented throughout the day. You make mental note of as much as you can, eager to practice your learnings on your next adventure.","e":["Each character gains 5 XP","Each character gains 5 XP"]}],[{"c":"C collective masteries completed","n":"You deliver a rousing explanation of combat mechanics peppered with real-world examples the other lecturers could only hope to experience. The audience is engrossed, and by the time you cede the floor, you feel a bit sorry for the presenter that has to follow you. Even when the audience erupts in applause, Argeise merely rolls her eyes, refusing to acknowledge your presentation skills.\n\n\"Don't let it go to your head, these soldiers are so green, they'd find the pommel of a sword fascinating. Anyway, here's payment for your presentation.\"","e":["Gain 15 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Military"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to speak to the class about your recent adventures, but they can tell you're about as experienced as they are. After a few minutes of fumbling, you wrap up your presentation and quickly make an exit.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Military"]}]],
    81: [[{"n":"You join hands with Hail and follow her lead. To your surprise, the destruction of the nexus takes little more than linking hands, some scrawled chalk outlines, chanting incantations in a tongue you don't understand, and watching a pair of boots disintegrate into a sparkle of dust.\n\n\"Whew, I don't think we're going to miss access to a random plane of wind!\" She claps her hands, turning to other tasks. You can't help but feel a sense of dread—who benefits from making it harder for visitors to come to your plane?","e":["Gain 3 reputation with Demons","Aesther starts the next scenario with curse."]}],[{"n":"\"Oh, you're no fun. Do you have any idea how long it took me to find these? So many mercenaries. Like, a lot of mercenaries. I even paid some of them in advance!\" She's losing you, but continues anyway.\n\n\"If someone else found our plane's nexus, they'd smash it in a heartbeat, let me tell you. Assuming they understand dimensional fragility and can channel a fulguration matrix. And good luck inventing those for another couple millennia, right?\" She laughs, then sees your blank stares. With a roll of her eyes she gives up. \"Sure, fine. Take 'em. See if I care.\"","e":["Gain item 114 Gust Striders"]}]],
    82: [[{"t":["strong","armored","intimidating"],"c":"Trait: Strong or Armored or Intimidating","n":"You stand your ground, and a few cracked jaws later, they've fallen back, still full of fire, but not willing to take a beating just to shout up-close. You get the foreman to safety, but not before locking eyes with the Bruiser, who could not look more furious at you.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice."]},{"o":1,"n":"You try to hold off the swarming crowd, but it's to no avail. What hurts more than the physical pain, though, is you're almost certain you saw your old friend the Bruiser's fist coming your way. The blows come quickly, and when they've had their fill, you're left with a ringing in your ears. Your employer is bloody, but thankfully alive. You drag him to safety and vow not to cross the dockworkers again.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice.","Scenario: start with Muddle"]}],[{"n":"\"See? Even your bodyguards know wrong when they see it!\" The dock foreman looks ashamed as you pass out the few coins you earned, but it's not enough. You reach into your own pocket to try to make the workers whole. The Bruiser approaches you with a sad smile. \"Thank you. It's not much, but it's the world to these people.\"","e":["Lose 5 collective gold"]}]],
    83: [[{"n":"One drink turns into five, and five turns into even more. It is a great night of revelry at the Sleeping Lion. You see sadness in the Cragheart's eyes when you finally stand up to leave. It tells you it's been hard to find people to relate to since leaving the party and it thanks you for your continued friendship.","e":["Each character loses 5 gold"]}],[{"n":"Not fitting in with its own kind or with a city of mostly humans, the Cragheart thought it could depend on a misfit group of mercenaries for friendship. It understands that its adventuring life is now in the past, though, and that it should go find a new place to belong. It sadly admits that it has no idea where that would be, but the Cragheart gets up and leaves the tavern nonetheless.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    84: [[{"n":"You take your last few minutes together to thank the Cragheart for its contributions to your mercenary party, and remind it that it always has a home with you if it needs it. It smiles a smile that makes clear it's appreciative, but that chapter is closed.\n\n\"Oh, that reminds me. I did find something that made me think of you. Perhaps it's of some use?\"","e":["Gain item 12 Stamina Potion","Event card road 57"]}],[{"n":"\"There is actually something I thought could be of use to you: I met a very old, very odd woman in an forest up north. She wouldn't speak, but she had a way about her. Necklace made of bark, if I recall. If you ever encounter her, treat her with respect—if I were you, I'd just lay down my weapons, to be frank. I think that would work out well for you.\" There's a smile, but it doesn't elaborate.","e":["Event card road 57"]}]],
    85: [[{"n":"It takes all of you in unison to exert enough force to snap the arcane scepter, but when you do, the energy released throws you to your knees. You don't know why your old friend had to die to protect it, but you will honor their wishes. Somehow, you hope they see your deed and find peace.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless","Lock scenario 94"]}],[{"n":"Even when they were still alive, you didn't always see eye-to-eye with the Soultether. You know that you have the strength to protect this staff, and you can put it to better use than being another discarded thing tossed aside. You will use it in their honor.","e":["Scenario: start with Curse","Gain item 139 Otherworldly Scepter","Lock scenario 94"]}]],
    86: [[{"n":"You try to reminisce with the Vermling about the Mindthief, but he's having none of it. \"Very sad. Droopy bones. Face like ooze, very sad.\" He pulls at his eye while frowning to demonstrate. \"So dead.\" After a few minutes, he excuses himself to check on some Black Imp stew he has cooking and forgets to return. You take the shawl and head to the Sleeping Lion to find other ways past your pain.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"t":["intimidating"],"c":"Trait: Intimidating","n":"You growl at the Vermling, pressing the issue. \"Fine, fine! They also left you some small money. No big deal, I would give. I give!\"","e":["Gain 15 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"You start to question the Vermling's retelling, but he loses interest in your interrogation. \"I see why they retired. Very see. You boring.\" He shuts the door.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    87: [[{"n":"\"The Vermlings have had success, so they'll return for more. Get there as soon as you can.\" Your old friend takes a long breath, then smiles. \"It was good seeing you—stay safe.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen","Unlock scenario 93"]}],[{"n":"You start to ask for payment, then remember that you don't actually need payment to help your old friend. If it's important to the Mindthief, it's important to you, and you would kindly help them whenever they ask. The Mindthief gives a knowing smile and you can't help but feel like you've forgotten something. No matter.\n\n\"The Vermlings have had success, so they'll return for more. Get there as soon as you can. No need to report back, I know you'll take care of it.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 93"]}]],
    88: [[{"n":"\"You are true friends. You are the anchor. I will not journey with you, but I will excise evil from this place in the shadows where you cannot.\"\n\nThe Nightshroud draws themselves to full height. You notice that, compared to a moment ago, they are a more healthy-looking opaque. Without additional ceremony, the Nightshroud vanishes in a twist of smoke.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}],[{"n":"\"I had purpose here. The draw was a life raft... but my purpose has concluded. I will not cling to that which has ended. A parting gift, then.\"\n\nThe Nightshroud touches your forehead, and you feel your mind tear for an instant. The dull thud lingers, but you feel something where there was nothing before. Without additional ceremony, the Nightshroud vanishes in a twist of smoke.","e":["Gain 2 battle goal checkmark(s)"]}]],
    89: [[{"t":["immunity"],"c":"Trait: Immunity","n":"You can't imagine any graveyard would accept it, so you make your way to the Void: the silent field of black sand in the middle of Gloomhaven that functions as a garbage dump for anyone that wants to dispose of something permanently. You toss the corpse in and watch it disintegrate.\n\nYou wish this was the first time you've encountered the Plagueherald's mess. Brushing off the fragments of black dust that landed on your clothes, you make your way over to the guard to collect the disposal payment.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Event card city 90"]},{"o":1,"n":"You can't imagine any graveyard would accept it, so you make your way to the Void: the silent field of black sand in the middle of Gloomhaven that functions as a garbage dump for anyone that wants to dispose of something permanently. You toss the corpse in and watch it disintegrate.\n\nYou collect the payment for the corpse removal from the guard and head back to your room, perspiration seeping into your clothes as your skin bubbles. Several days later you still feel sick and curse the Plagueherald for their involvement.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Scenario: start with Poison","Gain trait: Immunity"]}],[{"n":"Having witnessed the effects, you're not about to mess with whatever horrific disease the Plagueherald inflicted on that man. The guards curse you for leaving them to deal with it themselves.","e":["Lose 2 reputation with Military"]}]],
    90: [[{"n":"With the man dead at its feet, the Plagueherald makes a chittering sound that sounds almost like laughing. \"You cannot see it, but this city needs to be cleansed. You will see, and you will thank me.\" At this, the Plagueherald bursts out into a massive swarm of insects and flies up into the sky. The deaths continue, and new rumors start about how you are associated with the killer.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice.","Remove event card city 89"]}],[{"n":"The Plagueherald recoils at your attack, falling to the ground in a puddle of insects. \"But... the cleansing... the city isn't ready...\" You can't help but feel sorry at the sight of how far your friend has gone.\n\nIt chitters in disappointment, \"...You will be responsible when the Harbinger comes...\" The mass of bugs suddenly lurches spasmodically in on itself, finally relaxing. You kick the remainder apart with the toe of your boot, but there's nothing but curled up insect husks.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity","Trait: Immunity: Scenario: start with Safeguard","Remove event card city 89"]}]],
    91: [[{"n":"\"I know the condition you keep your equipment in, but still—a shortage is a shortage. What've you got?\"","e":["You may immediately sell any number of items for their full price."]}],[{"n":"You pick through the Quartermaster's cart, trying on various pieces of armor and testing the heft of the weapons. Perhaps some of this is suitable for use in the field.","e":["Each character may purchase one item from the available supply at half price."]}]],
    92: [[{"n":"It's a gift you couldn't have picked better yourself. You're closing out the night when you're approached by a hulking Savvas that introduces itself as an employee of Bonecruncher's.\n\n\"Sharing, eh? I'll let Bonecruncher know you're an additional guarantor of your friend's debt.\" The mountain of rock smiles. \"I'm sure it won't come to that, though.\"","e":["Each character may gain one item from the available supply that costs 25 gold or less.","Gain trait: Indebted","Event card city 38","Event card city 44"]}],[{"c":"Pay 100 collective gold","n":"Bonecruncher chuckles and happily accepts payment. Still, the Sawbones doesn't seem to appreciate the dire fate you avoided for them. \"I could've covered it, probably.\"","e":["Remove event card city 44"]},{"o":1,"n":"When you hear just how much the Sawbones owes, your eyes widen. You attempt to negotiate with Bonecruncher, who just chuckles. \"I'll tell you what: since you seem to care about this friend of yours, in the event the doc isn't able to pay the interest, I'll come find you instead of breaking their legs off. Seems like a good deal for your friend.\"","e":["Gain trait: Indebted","Event card city 38","Event card city 44"]}]],
    93: [[{"n":"You know how many people have been helped by the Sawbones, and it doesn't take much to brighten their spirits.\n\n\"You're right, I know I'm doing the right thing. And it's not the end of the road, right? I can contribute to Gloomhaven and still choose a new path someday in the future.\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}],[{"n":"You can see it in your old friend's face: they'll never be truly happy unless they scratch that wanderlust. If anything, it looks like they're asking for permission to do what they refuse to admit to themselves.\n\n\"You really think it'll be okay? I've given so much to this city, I just feel like it's time I did something for me, for a change.\" You tell them you'll support them no matter what, and the Sawbones looks like a weight has been lifted off them. \"You're right! I deserve to be happy!\"","e":["Event card city 92"]}]],
    94: [[{"t":["nimble"],"c":"Trait: Nimble","n":"You quickly scramble the lute's pegs before anyone notices. Basseloff takes to the stage, and the change causes enough of a stumble to impact his scores with the judges.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen","Apply outcome B"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to grab the lute, but a groupie quickly points you out. Before long, the crowd has turned against you, and you catch the eye of the Soothsinger as you're being carted off—they look exceptionally disappointed you didn't believe they could win without your \"help\".","e":["Scenario: start with Curse"]}],[{"n":"You know the Soothsinger's ability and would put them up against any challenger. Basseloff gave a fine performance, but the real entertainment begins when the Soothsinger takes the stage.\n\nThey're a commanding presence and launch directly into a power ballad. Suddenly, they change tempo into a bewildering instrumental, followed by intensifying amplitude and a grand finale that is a truly captivating performance. Your friend walks off triumphant from the contest. The judges cheer, screaming, \"Truly, Gloomhaven has proven it is a hub of great music!\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}]],
    95: [[{"t":["arcane"],"c":"Trait: Arcane","n":"Despite the early hour, you head down to the Inox's forge and get an incredibly strong fire going for him so he can complete his order. He seems very pleased at your proficiency.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"The Inox is completely dumbfounded when you walk all the way down to his forge, then proceed to exhibit zero aptitude at manipulating or controlling elemental energies. \"Thanks for, uh... nothing, I guess.\"","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}],[{"rp":["demons",9],"c":"Reputation with Demons above 9","n":"You inscribe a circle in ash at the base of the forge, and with a commanding boom, a Flame Demon appears before you. The Flame Demon obliges by producing gouts of fire as needed to support the Inox's work throughout the morning. When the task is complete, you thank the demon for its service, dismissing it back to the ether.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to summon a demon, but something has gone terribly awry. The Inox looks on in horror as his workshop is ravaged by the elements—it's clear the demons aren't interested in helping your cause. You apologize and sheepishly excuse yourself, leaving the Inox to clean up the mess.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}]],
    96: [[{"t":["arcane"],"c":"Trait: Arcane","n":"The Sunkeeper begins reciting long, elegant words you have not heard them use before in an unfamiliar tongue. You apply yourself to weaving energies, stitching the threads of bark like a costume over the tree. \"Thank you, friends. Enjoy its blessings—and remember, speak of this to no one.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]},{"o":1,"n":"The Sunkeeper enters a trancelike state, speaking words of unknown origin. You see sunlight exit their hands, drifting over the surface of the bark and weaving it back together. You try to provide support through sheer force of will, but before the gash seals, the Sunkeeper falls to the ground, exhausted. \"We'll leave it sealed off for now, and I'll return when I've recuperated. Thank you.\"","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You wait until midday when the sun is highest to give the tree the most energy. Rumor has it that boughs of the Great Oak refuse to burn, but it seems that the Oak supports your decision today and the kindling you pack into the wound rapidly catches light. You stoke the fire for a few hours, and when you clear off the charcoal, you find the gash has been successfully sealed off.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]}]],
    97: [[{"rp":["military",12],"c":"Reputation with Military above 12","n":"You're a known quantity as mercenaries, and the guard lets you off with a warning. The Sunkeeper gives a frustrated look. \"I've been tracking these crates for weeks, and this has been a huge waste of my time.\"","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"The guards arrive and are disappointed to just see you sheepishly sitting on a stack of crates. Your old friend does their best to explain the situation, and after a long back-and-forth, the Sunkeeper walks over to you. \"They can't ignore this, but they're willing to let you plead your case to the arbiters. Best I could do.\"","e":["Event card city 40"]}],[{"n":"\"Are you insane? Do you realize how much trouble you're in right now? I...\" The Sunkeeper, frustrated, sets down their warhammer. \"Go.\" You're gone before the guards arrive.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"\"Are you insane? Do you realize how much trouble you're in right now?\" The Sunkeeper, frustrated, holds you in the warehouse until backup arrives. It takes hours, but the guards finish processing the evidence and finally release you with a court date. The Sunkeeper shakes their head as you're lead outside.","e":["Event card city 40"]}]],
    98: [[{"n":"\"This can detect and hose down injured party members with suture spray. You're going to want to test-activate it a few times before trying it in the field. Last time, it wasted all of its healing acid spraying down a rock it thought was a Savvas. Melted it to slag. I'm almost certain I worked that kink out, though.\"","e":["Gain item 141 Remote Aid Spider"]}],[{"n":"\"Perfect, it should be calibrated to fire around you now. The abdomen will shoot out tiny darts on command. Originally I designed it to have eight tiny flamethrowers. Hah, well... it turns out friendly fire isn't.\"","e":["Gain item 140 Remote Attack Spider"]}]],
    99: [[{"c":"0 CARDS","n":"You easily deactivate the device.\n\n\"That was not supposed to happen. Although it does open up some interesting new scientific questions...\" Before you have a chance to inquire further, the Tinkerer wraps up the device and heads out, musing about potential upgrades.","e":["Gain 2 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"c":"1-2 CARDS","n":"You manage to deactivate the device, but it feels like a week has passed in the span of a second.\n\n\"That was not supposed to happen. Although it does open up some interesting new scientific questions...\" Before you have a chance to inquire further, the Tinkerer wraps up the device and heads out, musing about potential upgrades.","e":["Each character gains 10 XP"]},{"c":"3-5 CARDS","n":"Your uncoordinated attempts to deactivate the device leave you hitting and re-hitting buttons. When you're finally finished, the fire has spread to most of the room.\n\n\"That was not supposed to happen. Although it does open up some interesting new scientific questions...\" Before you have a chance to inquire further, the Tinkerer wraps up the device and heads out, musing about potential upgrades.","e":["Lose 5 collective gold"]},{"c":"5+ CARDS","n":"You slap at your fellow mercenaries' hands, attempting to deactivate the machine in a clumsy ballet of failure. When it finally clicks off, the fire started in your room has consumed a number of your personal belongings.\n\n\"That was not supposed to happen. Although it does open up some interesting new scientific questions...\" Before you have a chance to inquire further, the Tinkerer wraps up the device and heads out, musing about potential upgrades.","e":["Lose 15 collective gold"]}]],
    100: [[{"n":"\"Good, we'll need some supplies. Food, mostly. We need to attract some friends.\" They scramble up the window ledge, then pause before popping through. \"And more jerky. I'll meet you up there.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 84"]}],[{"n":"\"Hmph. Well, there's good reason I stick to the wilds. At least if you feed someone, you get some measure of loyalty.\" The Wildfury leaves the way they came, and fresh-sawn logs continue to flow into Gloomhaven.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}]],
  },
  road: {
    1: [[{"ta":["arcane","intimidating"],"c":"Every character has: Arcane, Intimidating","n":"You spin a tale of true terror. The fire flares up at the just the right times, then descends to near blackness when the mood requires. The travelers have trouble sleeping, and the following morning ask you to escort them to their destination for a fee-on the condition you don't tell any more stories.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to tell a scary tale, but after some snickers, it's clear you didn't frighten anyone at all.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"ta":["educated","persuasive"],"c":"Every character has: Educated, Persuasive","n":"You spin a tale of fantastic adventure, recapping the travels of a group similar to your own. You sprinkle in true facts from the region and smart anecdotes that paint the tale with an air of realism so strong it surely must be true. The mouths hanging open at the shocking conclusion are better than any applause. They ask that you join them for as long as you're heading the same direction to share more of your epic tales, and they're happy to pay for the company.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Scenario: start with Ward"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to tell a grand tale of adventure, but it winds up a jumbled mess of improbable situations and long-winded explanations. They're polite in their response, and you part ways the next morning.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    2: [[{"n":"A Lurker is still a formidable adversary, even with one leg immobilized. But you come at it from multiple sides and after a few good blows it falls, defeated.","e":["Each character gains 5 XP","Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"t":["armored","nimble","strong"],"c":"Trait: Armored or Nimble or Strong","n":"The Lurker doesn't seem to fully understand you're assisting and struggles throughout the process, lashing out wherever it can. It takes some coordinated effort, but you manage to distract the beast long enough to pry the trap from its leg.\n\nThe Lurker, confused, gives a final twist of its head before galloping into the stream. You'll interpret that as a \"thank you,\" which will perhaps ease the lacerations it left you with.","e":["Scenario: suffer 1 damage","Scenario: start with Bless:2"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to pacify the beast long enough to get closer to the trap, but the Lurker is having none of it. Finally, you commit to being beaten around the head with its terrifying claws while you pry the metal jaws free. It takes a final swipe at you before diving into the shallow river.","e":["Scenario: suffer 2 damage","Scenario: start with Bless:2"]}]],
    3: [[{"n":"\"Hey, that actually feels… better. I might be uncursed!\" He gives a celebratory jump, but stubs his toe on a rock in the process. \"Maybe still a little unlucky.\"","e":["Check a box below. The party may then collectively remove any number of bless cards from their attack modifier decks to check that many boxes. Finally, one character may gain one additional curse to check one additional box.","Scenario: start with Curse","Tick a box"]},{"c":"Check the third box","e":["Read section 17.3."],"r":1},{"c":"Check the last box","e":["Read section 34.4."]}],[{"n":"You deal a final, merciful blow, and the Quatryl falls peacefully. You can't help but feel that some of whatever afflicted him has washed off on you, though…","e":["Scenario: start with Curse"]}]],
    4: [[{"t":["outcast"],"c":"Trait: Outcast","n":"\"Last thing I need is word to get around. You look like someone with a closed jaw. Heh.\"","e":["Reduce the price below by 2 gold."]},{"c":"Pay 20 collective gold","n":"You may purchase any one of the below items. If you do, check the box and read the associated entry in the section book. When all boxes are checked, remove this event from the road deck.","e":["Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box"]}],[{"rp":["military",12],"c":"Reputation with Military above 12","n":"You engage the traveling merchant on how well-connected you are, but in the course of the conversation, something clicks, and he narrows his eyes. \"Store's closed. Sold out. Go away.\"","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"Glad to hear it.\"","e":["Apply outcome A","Reduce the price by 2 gold."]}]],
    5: [[{"c":"Pay 5 collective gold","n":"The wagon ride isn't luxurious, but it sure beats having to walk yourself. You arrive at your destination well-rested and ready for whatever circumstances are thrown at you.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen"],"r":1},{"o":1,"e":["Apply outcome B"]}],[{"n":"You wave the man off. You've arrived under your own power every time before, and today won't be any different. What's the worst that could happen?","e":["Draw another event card"]}]],
    6: [[{"n":"They head towards the smoking mountain, and a few days later at sunset, you feel an uneasy stillness, as though the mountain has finally come to rest. Odd.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You demand to take the young woman's place. The Savvas deliberate with each other for a moment, then acquiesce. \"Retrieve the sacred artifacts and cast the greater into the liquid flame so the mountain will rest. Fail, and you have doomed our village and this land.\"","e":["Unlock scenario 90"]}],[{"n":"The woman's captors are no match for trained mercenaries, but she is less than appreciative.\n\n\"You've doomed us! Now the mountain will flow with liquid flame and destroy my village!\" She falls to her knees, sobbing. In an attempt to pacify her, you agree to complete the ritual in her party's stead.\n\n\"Really? You'll need to push past the guardians to retrieve the sacred artifacts. Take the greater of the two and cast it into the mountain's fires. Oh, and I'm told a sacrifice of innocent blood will help appease the beast.\" You nod, but make no promises about that last part.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Unlock scenario 90"]}]],
    7: [[{"c":"If you draw a minus1 or lower card","n":"You pull up a chunk of half-eaten meat.","e":["No effect"]},{"c":"If you draw a plus0 card","n":"You find some discarded jewelry in the stream.","e":["Each character gains 2 gold"]},{"c":"If you draw a plus1 or higher card","n":"You pull a massive homefish from the stream.","e":["Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"c":"If you draw a double card","n":"It puts up a fight, but you reel in an iridescent gimmelfish.","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"c":"If you draw a null card","n":"The nibble at the end of your line suggests a tasty lunch is about to be served, but you didn't realize who was on the menu. When the rows of scalpel-like teeth burst from the edge of the stream, the idyllic fishing spot turns to a traumatic race for cover. Tentacles whip sludge-filled barbs at anything within terrifying range. The eye-stalk breaches the water last: a crimson orb hunting you down among the tall grass.\n\nYou regain your wits and defend yourself, finally taking down the deep terror, but it will be weeks before you wake up in anything but a cold sweat.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Each character individually chooses to start the next scenario with immobilize or disarm."]}]],
    8: [[{"t":["armored","intimidating","strong"],"c":"Trait: Armored or Intimidating or Strong","n":"You fight through the unbearable urge to sleep. You make a hasty retreat—but you make note of the location to return someday better prepared.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle","Unlock scenario 97"]},{"o":1,"n":"The only thing keeping you awake is the punctures of spearpoints as you attempt to retreat. You manage to make it to safety and note the location for the future. Whether it's the blood loss or the poison you're not sure, but you are due for a nap.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle","Unlock scenario 97"]}],[{"t":["nimble","strong"],"c":"Trait: Nimble or Strong","n":"With heavy eyelids, you grab the handle of the mace and start running, dodging projectiles as you go. You mark the location to return someday.","e":["Gain item 51 Heavy Mace","Unlock scenario 97"]},{"o":1,"n":"You grab the handle of the mace, but it's heavier than it looks. With the extra weight, a poorly-timed nap is in your future.","e":["Apply outcome A","Scenario: suffer 3 damage"]}]],
    9: [[{"t":["educated"],"c":"Trait: Educated","n":"A cursory look is all it takes to confirm your suspicion: the piston chamber is losing pressure due to icing at higher altitudes. It's a small matter to better insulate the valve and the system is again flight-worthy. You stand clear and watch in awe as the thing begins flapping wildly and lifts off the ground.","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]},{"o":1,"n":"It's pretty clear what the problem is: there isn't a feather anywhere on the thing. The leather is from ground-based animals and wood also grows out of the ground. The Quatryl sighs as you explain it to him. \"…right. Okay, I'll just finish this one on my own. Thanks.\"\n\nA short time later you see the machine scream past above you. Unfortunately, the flight is short-lived, and the second crash is not nearly as forgiving. You find the Quatryl dead on impact, and there's nothing more to do except harvest the machine for valuable parts. You did try to warn him.","e":["Gain a random item design"]}],[{"n":"You set the wings and bang out a few dents while the Quatryl repairs his pressure problem. In under an hour the Quatryl declares the contraption airworthy and jumps in the cockpit. Unfortunately, the flight is short-lived, and the second crash is not nearly as forgiving. You find the Quatryl dead on impact, and there's nothing more to do except harvest the machine for valuable parts.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}]],
    10: [[{"n":"You may touch any one crystal."},{"c":"Blue triangle crystal","e":["Read section 76.5."]},{"c":"Red circular crystal","e":["Read section 66.5."]},{"c":"Orange hex crystal","e":["Read section 122.1."]},{"c":"Green diamond crystal","e":["Read section 135.5."]}],[{"n":"You press the big button in the center of the console. The system whirrs to life, the lights dancing in a pattern beyond your comprehension. A voice rings inside your head, but you can't find the source of the sound.\n\n\"This is Qualco's Temporal Stash, keep out! This stash made possible through lots of trial and error and error and also some help from a pair of helpful Aesthers. But this is for Qualco's eyes only! Since time is a bit wobbly, I'll remind you—ME, Qualco only!—of the most important rule: No crystal is pressed more than once!\"\n\n\"But future-Qualco: if you do manage to get it wrong, that'll discharge the crystal matrix, reset the stash's location, and initiate defense measures. Take that, any not-Qualcos! I said for Qualco's eyes only and I mean it!\"","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]},{"n":"You may touch any one crystal."},{"c":"Blue triangle crystal","e":["Read section 70.4."]},{"c":"Red circular crystal","e":["Read section 82.5."]},{"c":"Orange hex crystal","e":["Read section 119.4."]},{"c":"Green diamond crystal","e":["Read section 98.5."]}]],
    11: [[{"n":"You shrug and grab a handful of berries to stuff in your mouth. They are incredibly sweet and just the right amount of tart. You couldn't feel better about your decision. That is, until you start vomiting. Your stomach is incredibly unhappy with you, and the situation doesn't improve much by the time you arrive at your destination.","e":["Scenario: start with Poison"]}],[{"n":"Not wanting to regret making a stupid decision, you refrain from eating the berries and continue on down the road.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    12: [[{"c":"Pay item 12 Stamina Potion","n":"After some oddly tense negotiations, you are able to agree upon a price. With one hand firmly on his sword hilt, the man grabs a coin pouch with the other hand and extends it toward you. You exchange goods and continue on your journey without further incident.","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Gain 10 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"e":["Apply outcome B"]}],[{"t":["outcast"],"c":"Trait: Outcast","n":"There was something off-putting about that man. You are more than happy to move along and put some distance between you.\n\nIt feels good to snub that mercenary. Is that how they feel when they look at you? Empowering, really.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen"]},{"o":1,"n":"There was something off-putting about that man. You are more than happy to move along and put some distance between you.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    13: [[{"n":"He speaks slowly and softly: \"Gloomhaven is a troubled city... I hope to speak with the leadership there. I only hope that my warnings will not fall on deaf ears.\" He gives a somber look. \"Sometimes all that's required is a friendly introduction...\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity","Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]}],[{"n":"He speaks slowly and softly: \"Your journey is nearly at an end, but there are others like you that will take up your standard. Your upcoming retirement will be arguably as good as you dream, but I fear adversity looms in the change.\"\n\nYou turn to leave, but he calls you back. \"Oh, one more thing: be wary in your upcoming travels. I foresee that a minor injury will prevent a more serious incident. Good luck.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    14: [[{"n":"The sticky brambles scratch and tear whatever gets within reach, and in short order, you're covered in pinpricks. When you do finally make it up to the outpost, you're dead tired. You hope that a future trip is made easier by your efforts, but you can't help but grumble at how much work it was for so little reward.\n\nYou're back on your way shortly before sunrise, sore muscles and all.","e":["Event card road 31","Discard 2","Scenario: suffer 1 damage","Scenario: start with Wound","Each armored character ignores the suffer 1 damage and wound."]}],[{"n":"Bushwhacking the sticky brambles is frustrating work. While it may just be your imagination, you can nearly feel the bushes regrowing behind you. Several hours of work later, you emerge on the other side of the thicket and resume your journey.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    15: [[{"rp":["demons",12],"c":"Reputation with Demons above 12","n":"You brazenly confront the flame demons, ordering them to stand down. They recognize you and tone down the heat, but most of the crop is already lost. They eventually depart, leaving you to sort through the remains of the farmer's home and crops.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow","Gain 15 collective gold"]},{"o":1,"n":"The demons don't take kindly to your tone. There isn't anything left of the farmer's home by the time the fight is over, but you do find a few fruits still intact.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow","Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"n":"It doesn't look like there's any reason to get involved defending a dead man. You pick a few of the ripest looking fruits from the trees and depart before the rest of the orchard burns down.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow"]}],[{"n":"Pursued by the flame demons, you hastily make your way into the burning building, gathering whatever valuables you can find. Soot and ash rain down on you as the thatched roof ignites. It takes everything you have to beat back the demons in the chaos and make it out with your lives.","e":["Gain 15 collective gold","Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    16: [[{"c":"Lose 5, 9, 26, 59, or 149","n":"You dismantle your possession and, with a bit of effort, are able to repair the damaged telescope. \"See there? That twinkling teal crystal budding right out of the soil on the moon?\" She makes some excited marks in her journal. \"It's growing. I've been observing it every few centuries. But the real interesting part? When the moon rotates clear around to the other side, there's another one, straight across from each other if you drew a line through the core.\"\n\nShe stretches her back with a crack that sounds decades in the making. \"Two crystals, opposite sides of a moon that'll never get the chance to see each other. Who put them there? I have my theories. Maybe it's nothing. Or maybe it'll be very important someday.\"","e":["Each character gains 15 XP","Gain trait: Educated"]},{"o":1,"e":["Apply outcome B"]}],[{"n":"\"Gloomhaven? Miserable name for a city, just dreadful. Things really have changed while I was asleep!\" You draw her a crude map of the region and showcase where Gloomhaven sits at the mouth of the Still River. She raises an eyebrow, but doesn't explain why. \"Well, thank you for the help.\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    17: [[{"t":["persuasive"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive","n":"After a rousing pep talk, the young man gives a somber nod and heads into the mouth of the cave. You wait a few minutes for his return, but with the sun setting soon, you head off towards your destination.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You give an explanation of how his cowardice will haunt him for the rest of his life, but it doesn't overcome his fear of entering the dark cave. After more than an hour of attempts, you leave him to build up the courage himself.","e":["Discard 1"]}],[{"t":["outcast"],"c":"Trait: Outcast","n":"You explain to the boy that those \"friends\" were bullies, and that he's better off without them. He eventually nods his understanding and starts the walk back to Gloomhaven, alone. It feels like you inspired something in the boy.","e":["Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"o":1,"n":"You take pity on the boy's circumstances and escort him in, ready to get the jump on these \"friends\" that are so willing to bully him. The cave is surprisingly deep—and then the growling starts. Two full-grown cave bears are finishing up a meal, but they have room for dessert. It's a bloody fight, but you emerge victorious.\n\nThe boy, although unharmed, looks pretty shaken up.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    18: [[{"n":"You pen a short missive confirming everything is on schedule and tie it onto the raven's other leg. It is seemingly waiting for something, and after a moment, you break off a piece of your trail ration. Satisfied, it takes to the air, and you quickly lose sight of it amongst the tree tops. Oh well.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You write a short note explaining that this bird seems to have confused you with someone else. You sign at the bottom and tie it to the bird, giving it a few pats on the head. It looks confused, but eventually takes off. A few hours down the trail, you come across a black leather coin purse, seemingly left for you.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"As a former Sin-Ra operative, you know their methods when you see them. You write a return note and carefully—carefully place a single drop of concentrated poison in the folds. You tie it to the raven, and with a sharp whistle, you order it back into the air.\n\nA few hours down the trail, you come across a dead man in the road, the note clutched in his hand. With one less operative in the world, you take what you can and move on.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold","Gain a random item design"]}]],
    19: [[{"t":["resourceful","nimble"],"c":"Trait: Resourceful or Nimble","n":"You always keep a few pins around in case you need to open something you shouldn't. You easily pick the lock, finding only a notebook and a small mechanical bell—which begins clanging loudly.\n\n\"THIEVES!\" cries the Valrath, ripping the box from your hands before riding away on his exhausted hristek. \"I'll take my chances on my own.\"","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Demons"]},{"o":1,"n":"Your clumsy efforts to pick the lock disturb the hristek, who honks angrily. You pretend you were merely petting the animal, and the traveler laughs. \"Yes, she dislikes strangers, I'm afraid.\"","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"The traveler's business is his own, and besides, you're curious—what brings a lone rider into the dangerous wilds? \"I'm a scout,\" the Valrath confides, \"I work for a secret group that will bring salvation to Gloomhaven.\"\n\n\"If you're of like mind, simply look for the symbol of the trident, and together we'll save our city.\"","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Demons"]}]],
    20: [[{"n":"The prisoners are already worse for wear from the long walk, and it doesn't take much to subdue them. You make sure the manacles are in place before you bid the guards a good day. They nod their thanks and are sure to let you know they'll put in a good word with their superiors.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military"]}],[{"n":"In a flash, the prisoners rush past you and into the cover of the trees. It's perfectly plausible that you just didn't react quickly enough, but that doesn't save you from the admonishment of the guards.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Military"]}]],
    21: [[{"n":"The operator shows you how to use the slot machine, and sets you up to pull the lever. He hands you a drink with chunks of ice floating in it. Tasty.","e":["Make an 8-card slot machine deck composed of attack modifier deck cards from the ally modifier deck: two minus1s, two plus1s, two plus1s, and any two other attack modifier cards of your choice. Each character may pull the slot machine lever as many times as they choose. For each pull, pay 5 gold and draw three cards from the slot machine deck. If two cards match, that character gains 4 gold. If all three cards match, instead gain 20 gold. If all three cards match three times in a row, also gain a random item design. Otherwise, gain nothing. Shuffle the slot machine deck after each pull.\n\nThe Quatryl looks delighted with your participation. \"I'm also happy to discuss Slot Sanctum franchise opportunities!\""]}],[{"t":["quatryl"],"c":"Trait: Quatryl","n":"You ask for a tour of how the marvelous machine works, and the Quatryl is more than happy to showcase it.","e":["Apply outcome A","Add two additional attack modifier cards of your choice to the machine."]},{"o":1,"n":"The Quatryl notices your attempt to distract him and chides you for the attempt. \"I regret to inform you that you'll need to leave the Slot Sanctum premises for violating protocol. Good day!\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    22: [[{"e":["Read section 37.3."]}],[{"n":"There are reasons for adventure, and those exist at your destination. No need to stray unnecessarily.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    23: [[{"n":"You deal a swift, mortal wound. As he expires, a weak smile dresses his face, and he whispers, \"she was telling the truth. I saved him... Thank you...\"","e":["Each character gains 5 XP"]}],[{"n":"\"No, you must do it! You must! I spent fifty years away from my son! My boy! If you don't finish this, it was all for nothing!\" He breaks down sobbing, begging you to meet his request.\n\nYou turn away from the troubled man and continue on your way. His choices were certainly unfortunate, but ultimately not your concern.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    24: [[{"c":"All players said \"G\"","n":"You each reach out simultaneously to grip the valve's handle, wrenching it in unison. It seals with a groan, and with the water stopped, you're able to pry open the hatch and make your way back to the surface.","e":["Each character gains 10 XP"]},{"o":1,"n":"There's no time to think, but it turns out there is a way to make the situation worse: the lever you selected increases the rapid flow of water into the room. You're soaked and exhausted by the time you're able to pry the rusted hatch open.","e":["Discard 2"]}]],
    25: [[{"n":"You're still climbing the trunk of the enormous tree when you feel the tug at your feet—the skeleton is clawing at you! It pulls you to the ground and while it's no match for you, it still fights with a terrifying intensity. You scatter the bones and continue to your destination.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow","Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"c":"Pay 5 collective gold","n":"You drop five coins in the bucket and make your way up to the low branches of the tree where you find the most perfect specimen, packing it along with you. The skeleton pays you no mind.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow"]},{"o":1,"e":["Apply outcome A"]}],[{"n":"You reach in and pull out a handful of gold coins—you're not sure why someone left them here, but before you can pocket them, the skeleton in overalls leaps at you with a terrifying intensity. You beat it back and hurry to your destination, leaving the coins behind.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    26: [[{"n":"You strip the finery off the Savvas corpse, taking special care to keep the lapel pin identifying it as a member of the Merchant's Guild. The sun is setting by the time you've finished burying the corpse in a better grave, but you should be able to sell the belongings for a high price when you return to town.","e":["Gain 30 collective gold","Discard 1"]}],[{"n":"You wrap the body in a blanket and cinch it tight with rope, throwing it over your shoulder. It's as heavy as a corpse made of rock, but you think you can manage. How hard could it be?\n\nFor the next scenario, select one character to carry the body. That character adds three minus1 cards to their attack modifier deck for the scenario.","e":["If you successfully complete the scenario: Read section 127.2","Read section 78.5"]}]],
    27: [[{"t":["chaotic"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic","n":"You gather a handful of leaves and walk over to him. You lock eyes with the man throughout the encounter. It makes it significantly more awkward for everyone.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You gather a handful of leaves and walk over to him. If you weren't quite sure what was going on before, the smell definitely confirms it.\n\n\"Thanks a lot!\" He says cheerily. \"Sometimes nature calls, am I right?\"\n\nYou cough in affirmation and quickly move on.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"You look from the squatting man down to his guard clothes. Surely he has something of value, but even if not—humiliating a guard can be its own reward. You quickly grab it and run off down the road.\n\n\"Hey!\" The man yells at you. \"What are you doing? That's city property!\"\n\nYou don't look back.","e":["Each character gains 5 gold","Lose 1 reputation with Military"]}]],
    28: [[{"t":["strong","intimidating"],"c":"Trait: Strong or Intimidating","n":"You drag their leader off the wagon and with a swift motion, unhitch the cart door to bury him in amberhollow. It takes just a swift kick and the fragile fruit ruptures in a loud detonation—the chain reaction leaves him drenched in sweet liquid. He looks like he's about to say something, then shifts his stance and walks off without a word, his stunned goons following quickly behind.\n\nThe farmer's wife stifles a laugh of her own, and they gift you a thank-you before leaving with the remainder of their harvest.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow","Scenario: start with Safeguard","Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]},{"o":1,"n":"You try to stand up to the Four Crosses, but the conversation quickly turns to mimicry and mockery. You refuse to meet them on their level and head off to your destination.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]}],[{"n":"You remind the farmers that the Four Crosses are the rightful owners of half the wagon's bounty, leaving them to silently seethe. The mohawked brawler grunts. \"You dumb idiots aren't so bad. Have one on us.\"","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow","Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]}]],
    29: [[{"n":"You pluck a few green berries off the branches to stuff in your mouth. They are incredibly sweet and just the right amount of tart.\n\nAn Orchid farmer plods by on the road beside you leading a kivak carrying baskets of the green berries. \"Enjoying the harvest?\" He gives a stiff pat to the rocky skin on the side of the kivak, sending it off into the berries to find lunch. \"Tin-berries only ripen once every three years. The red ones are darned poisonous until they turn that pretty green, but once they do... OOH-wee! Best roadside snack you can find outside of an amberhollow tree.\"\n\nHe plucks a few choice clusters and stows them in a pouch. \"Enjoy it while you can, these bushes'll die off once they've been picked clean. It'll be ages before we see them again.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Bless","Remove event card road 11"]}],[{"n":"Not wanting to regret making a stupid decision, you refrain from eating the berries and continue on down the road. A moment later you squeeze past an Orchid farmer walking a kivak down the narrow path. He tips his hat in passing. \"Make sure you try the green tin-berries while you can!\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    30: [[{"n":"The party may lose 15 collective gold to check one box below and gain the corresponding item.","e":["Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box","Tick a box"],"r":1},{"c":"All six boxes have been checked","x":1}]],
    31: [[{"n":"You follow the trail up to the abandoned outpost you discovered and settle in for an easy evening. There's still wood stocked in the shed, and the view out the windows demonstrates the beauty of the landscape around Gloomhaven. You don't know who owns this place, but routine maintenance goes a long way to making the surroundings more hospitable.\n\nBefore settling into bed, you rummage through the gardens and find some fresh amberhollow ripening on a tree.","e":["Gain item 146 Amberhollow","Scenario: start with Bless","Gain 1 prosperity","Event card road 14"]}],[{"n":"You head down the bushwhacked path towards your destination. The work that you'd done in the past pays off today, and keeping the surroundings hospitable has likely helped many travelers on their way to Gloomhaven.\n\nThe rest of your trip is uneventful and you arrive ready for whatever is thrown at you.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen","Gain 1 prosperity","Event card road 14"]}]],
    32: [[{"n":"You stand by as the drake takes a single, devastating bite. The top half of the Inox is cleanly removed, and the drake makes small talk as he finishes the remainder. When the conversation naturally reaches a close, he takes off with a wave of his wing.\n\n\"Come see me any time!\"","e":["Gain item 120 Drakescale Armor"]}],[{"n":"\"You wish me to... spare him?\" You explain that with such a generous gift, the Inox has already proven his value. The drake ponders this for a few tense moments. \"Very well. I will forgive your transgression, and you will never again set foot in the Copperneck Mountains. Mercenaries, enjoy the armor—it is truly one of its kind.\" With that, the drake takes flight and is gone.\n\nThe Inox falls to his knees, wiping tears out of his eyes. \"Thank you! Thank you! How can I ever repay you?\"\n\nIt turns out the Inox really is an excellent smith, and he spends the next few hours sharpening and polishing your equipment.","e":["Gain item 120 Drakescale Armor","Scenario: start with Strengthen"]}]],
    33: [[{"n":"You awkwardly thank her for the sword, but steer clear of confirming her belief that you are a chosen... well, anything. She stands after a too-long period, wiping tears from her joyous eyes. \"You will do great things! Thank you for your sacrifices. My husband's spirit will rest knowing his essence enabled your calling.\" She apologies for taking up so much of your precious time, leaving you with a sword of exceptional craftsmanship.","e":["Gain item 118 Duskbrand","Scenario: start with Muddle","Event card road 34"]}],[{"n":"With all of the reverence due to someone whose husband cast himself into a forge on the mistaken belief that you were somehow chosen to wield a blade you basically nabbed as compensation for clearing an elemental factory, you explain that you are not actually whatever chosen person she believes you to be. She cuts you off with a wave of her hand.\n\n\"The chosen demonstrates such humility! May the blade destroy your enemies, for there are many, and your trials impossible to fathom. You will do great things!\"","e":["Gain item 118 Duskbrand","Scenario: start with Ward","Event card road 34"]}]],
    34: [[{"n":"You draw the twin swords and hold them out for inspection. The Vermlings' eyes widen at the sight, huge smiles playing across their faces.\n\n\"It is true! We are so sorry for the sacrifices you have made to acquire them, and the sacrifices yet to come for you. Bless you, truly. We won't interrupt your quest any further!\" With that, they rush off.\n\nYou really need to find out where Xain got those blueprints.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless","Event card road 35"]}],[{"n":"The Vermlings appear understanding, and nod with a borderline conspiratorial tone. \"Yes, yes—we wouldn't want such powerful artifacts to fall into the wrong hands. That's wise of you.\" The whole exchange is quite awkward, and you can't help but feel that they're judging you, although they make no overt suggestion that's true. They cinch up their robes and, after some light conversation, proceed down a different trail. The one at the rear mutters something and you feel a sense of dread permeate the air.\n\nYou really need to find out where Xain got those blueprints.","e":["Scenario: start with Curse","Event card road 35"]}]],
    35: [[{"n":"You speak in vague terms about your personal relationship with Bonecruncher, leaving Xain turning paler by the minute. He nervously shifts his weight when you mention just how simple it'd be to tip off his creditor. \"Alright, alright, fine! Listen, I'm skipping town in part because I don't have money. But here, fine, take it. It's all I've got. I'm sure I'll be able to get rich quick up in Frosthaven anyway—people'll be tripping over themselves to invest in my ideas.\"","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}],[{"n":"You explain that, ever since you forged the Dawnblade with Sunny's help, you've been accosted by confused emissaries. He raises an eyebrow, taking it all in.\n\n\"The blueprints? I just bought them off an old Vermling. He said he'd nabbed it off some dead mercenaries. Nothing to it...\" Xain's face brightens, an idea forming. \"...unless it's really valuable to you, in which case, I feel obliged to mention the finder's fee you owe me.\" You give him a look and he shrinks a bit.\n\n\"What? I've got a long trip ahead of me. Everyone's got to eat. Except Savvas. And Aesthers. And uh, Orchids like me, I guess. But still, you get it.\" You begrudgingly hand him a couple coins just to end the conversation.","e":["Lose 5 collective gold"]}]],
    36: [[{"c":"Each character has at least one card in their card pool with an elemental infusion","n":"You summon your own power to hold the hungry rift at bay. Sure enough, your spells spin lazily around the portal's rim, slowly draining into its center. That should hold it for a while.","e":["Each character gains 5 XP"],"r":1},{"o":1,"n":"This place is lost already, and a random stretch of wilderness isn't worth your time. You wade through the gathering ash as you head back to the road.","e":["No effect"],"r":1}],[{"n":"You leap through the rift and find yourself in the palace of the Prime Demon Ka'athrash on the Elemental Plane of Power. Floating before you in a chamber of pure white stone is the source of the trouble: an obsidian amulet in the shape of a bird's skull. The elemental streams flow endlessly into it, but it craves ever more. You can feel it pulling at your own energy too, offering a trade: your essence for its power. You take it with you... you're sure the Prime Demon won't miss it.","e":["Gain item 128 Pendant Of Dark Pacts","Discard 2"]}]],
    37: [[{"n":"\"It's settled, then. You two!\" She calls over her two hulking guards. \"Guard these mercenaries with your lives. They're doing something very important today for the Merchant's Guild, and you'll see it through to your end.\" She starts heading back to her skeleton-drawn wagon, tail swishing behind her.\n\nYou lead them a short distance into the forest and spring the attack. The duo return blow after blow, but after a few frantic minutes, you're dragging their bodies back to Jekserah.\n\nShe passes over a red leather sack of gold. \"I do appreciate your loyalty.\"","e":["Gain 20 collective gold","Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Each character gains 5 XP","Scenario: suffer 3 damage","Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"n":"You're mercenaries, not hitmen. You turn down the Valrath, who doesn't take kindly to being told no.\n\n\"Well... I do appreciate your loyalty.\"","e":["Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild","Scenario: start with Ward"]}]],
    38: [[{"rp":["demons",3],"c":"Reputation with Demons above 3","n":"The summoning sigil manifests a dozen terrifying demons. The caster calls to them in a guttural tongue, and, while you don't see the demons respond in any discernible way, he seems satisfied.\n\n\"They confirm your claims. You are free to go.\" The demons recede into the sigil, and the barrier drops. You still elect to choose a new place to camp.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"We have borne witness to your transgressions. Now you will suffer our wrath!\" The fight drives you to the brink of exhaustion, mentally pleading for the pain to end. You finally drive your weapon into the last of the demons—the caster is conveniently nowhere to be found.","e":["Scenario: suffer 2 damage","Scenario: start with Wound","Discard 1"],"r":1}],[{"n":"The fight starts in an instant, but lasts several minutes of grueling, life-threatening combat. By the end, you've nearly exhausted the tricks up your sleeve. Thankfully, your final adversary is as weakened as you are, and with a bit of coordination, you manage to end it. The sigil burns away and the barrier drops, but the caster is conveniently nowhere to be found. Crossing the demons may be hazardous to your health.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Discard 1"]}]],
    39: [[{"t":["herald of xorn"],"c":"Trait: Herald Of Xorn","n":"You address the sea of insects. Slowly, arduously, the army of tiny dots accumulate. \n\nA black ocean of chitin swells at your command. With a thought, you order their assistance, and they flood over you and your companions, bestowing the gift of Xorn.","e":["Each character adds poison to all of their attacks performed during the first round of the next scenario","Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)","Scenario: start with Muddle"]},{"o":1,"n":"A wave of sticky black legs tear at you. You rush through to the other side, slapping at your body and hoping the pain subsides.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"t":["nimble"],"c":"Trait: Nimble","n":"You quietly make your way through the forest, crushing a minimal number underfoot.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"To your horror, the army of tiny dots swells into mounds of undulating limbs. They extend their appendages at you as you rush through, trying to hold your mouth shut lest they climb inside.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    40: [[{"t":["persuasive","educated"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive or Educated","n":"You expertly comment at length about how he's trying to compensate with his physique, but you both know it isn't even that impressive. The Orchid sits on a stump, staring at the ground quietly until you depart.","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"o":1,"n":"This Orchid is well-trained in being a jerk. He interrupts and peppers you with insults until you leave.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]}],[{"t":["strong"],"c":"Trait: Strong","n":"You lay into the trees with force borne of anger, and before long, you've cut down a sloppy pile of wood. Comparing it to the Orchid's, it's clear he's more skilled, but you win. \"Hmph, not bad, for city-folk.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"o":1,"n":"After ten minutes of effort, you finally concede defeat to the lumberjack, panting and exhausted. \"Not so easy, is it? Weak.\"","e":["Discard 2"]}],[{"n":"His chuckling ceases with a slow gurgle, your weapon piercing through his torso. You take a small delight in setting the cabin ablaze. It may not have been kind, but it was certainly deserved. One less antagonist in the world.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen","Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]}]],
    41: [[{"n":"A few sharp blows are all it takes to shatter the crystals encasing the rot, exposing the interior to cleansing sunlight. It writhes and burns away what's left, leaving nothing but dense black soot and a foul odor. You pile what's left of the dead Orchid into a funeral pyre and make sure it's burned away before leaving. It takes most of the afternoon, but the effort will hopefully prevent some other travelers from an untimely fate.","e":["Discard 1"]}],[{"t":["memory of serenity"],"c":"Trait: Memory Of Serenity","n":"You take the refined memory crystal you received from an Orchid in the Sleeping Lion and press it deep into the black ichor swirling inside the dead Orchid's head. Within seconds, the half-formed Crystal Rot starts to violently convulse, frustrated at the peaceful images forced into its angry mind. You watch as the serene memory refracts outward, cauterizing the liquid darkness in piercing shards of light. Its neck droops, and the figure collapses to the ground, finally at peace. You burn the corpse per Orchid tradition, and a calm washes over the landscape.","e":["Lose trait: Memory Of Serenity","Scenario: start with Bless","Gain 1 prosperity"]},{"o":1,"n":"You try to calm the feeding beast, but it seems riled by your presence—almost as if it can sense the lives you've taken hanging as an aura around you. It moves subtly, slowly, and then launches an attack with surprising force. You beat it to the ground and destroy the remains.","e":["Scenario: start with Curse"]}]],
    42: [[{"t":["savvas"],"c":"Trait: Savvas","n":"You take steady steps though the raging river, walking along the bottom until you reach the other side unharmed.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You are water-logged and still shivering from the icy river when you reach your destination.","e":["Scenario: start with Immobilize"]}],[{"t":["arcane"],"c":"Trait: Arcane","n":"With the power of the elements on your side, crossing the river turns out to be incredibly easy. One frozen bridge later, you are on the other side.","e":["No effect"]},{"t":["resourceful"],"c":"Trait: Resourceful","n":"It takes rocks, downed tree limbs, and all the twine from your satchel to make up the rickety bridge, but it holds long enough for you to make it safely across. You arrive at your destination tired but mostly dry.","e":["Discard 1"]},{"o":1,"n":"You assemble the best impromptu bridge you've ever built. Judging by the midway plunge into the icy river, though, it will also be the last.","e":["Each character starts the next scenario adding two minus1 cards into their attack modifier deck."]}]],
    43: [[{"t":["savvas","aesther"],"c":"Trait: Savvas or Aesther","n":"The pressure and inability to breathe would be unbearable if those were concerns for someone like you. At the bottom, you find what looks to be a meditating Savvas. You hitch your arms under and drag it to the surface.","e":["Read section 6.3"]},{"c":"Global achievement \"Into the depths\"","n":"The pressure and inability to breathe would be unbearable if those were concerns for someone like you. At the bottom, you find what looks to be a meditating Savvas. You hitch your arms under and drag it to the surface.","e":["Read section 6.3"]},{"t":["resourceful"],"c":"Trait: Resourceful","n":"With nothing but a loop of rope from your pack and a nearby rock, you manage to fashion an improvised fishing rod. After a few attempts, you manage to catch the end of the rope under the figure at the bottom of the pool and haul in what looks to be a meditating Savvas.","e":["Read section 6.3"]},{"o":1,"n":"Sure that it's too deep for you to swim down, you spend some time trying to fish out the figure with some rope (ineffective), and spear the figure out with a long stick (also ineffective). With the sun starting to set, you give up, vowing to return some other day.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle","Discard 1"],"r":1}],[{"n":"Sometimes figures hang out at the bottom of pools. Pools where the water flows the wrong direction. Big deal? There's enough oddities in this world that this one isn't worth your time.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    44: [[{"n":"Enter the rift.","e":["Scenario: suffer 1 damage","Flip a card (start over, and read event again)"]}],[{"n":"Refuse the call.","x":1}]],
    45: [[{"t":["aesther"],"c":"Trait: Aesther","n":"You recognize this illusion as an Aesther that has not yet managed to coalesce itself. Your own formation required fixation on a single, unifying ideal—she hasn't yet found her own anchor. You lend some of your focus, and a flicker of calm passes over her before she suddenly vanishes. You don't know if it's enough, but you hope you've shortened her trials.","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"o":1,"n":"You reach out to touch the glowing woman, but find yourself waking up with a pounding headache and covered in long claw marks an hour's walk from where you started. So much for helping.","e":["Scenario: suffer 2 damage","Scenario: start with Wound"]}],[{"n":"You sit at the water's edge through the night and watch the woman flicker in and out of reality, reaching for levers that don't exist, frantically pawing at invisible walls, and finally breaking down crying. She repeats the pattern over and over, and you catch words here and there: \"tower,\" \"seeker,\" but if there is no logic to the order.\n\nWhen the sun rises, the woman flickers a final time and vanishes. The old man gives it a solid ten seconds before he reaches into the pool and scoops up a cupful of glowing water, offering you some.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen"]}]],
    46: [[{"t":["nimble"],"c":"Trait: Nimble","n":"Your stealth skills prove sufficient to remain unnoticed by a group of night demons. They pass by without incident.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to hide and stay quiet, but a snapped twig at an unfortunate moment startles the a group of night demons, who immediately fly into an attack. The scene turns bloody, and you're barely able to fight them off.","e":["Scenario: suffer 3 damage"]}],[{"rp":["demons",9],"c":"Reputation with Demons above 9","n":"You can barely make them out against the pitch-black night, but in the firelight you see the silken, translucent forms of night demons approach. You wave them over to your campfire, but they seem content to stay at a respectful distance, watching the flames. When you next look up, they're gone.","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You wait by the fireside for your visitors. The night takes on an uneasy, stomach-corrupting feeling, and after a too-long pause, the fire extinguishes itself in a snap of smoke. Before you can react, the night demons are upon you, tearing at you under the moonless night. You fend them off, but arrive at your destination the next day still licking your wounds.","e":["Scenario: suffer 3 damage"]}]],
    47: [[{"t":["resourceful"],"c":"Trait: Resourceful","n":"You step forward, and with a bit of scrounging between your bags and the underbrush, you're able to put together a pretty decent sack of food and gear. The Valraths are grateful for the aid, and promise to sing your praises.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice."]},{"o":1,"n":"You'll need to replace the supplies next time you're in town, but you decide you can spare them. The Valraths breathe a sigh of relief, thanking you and promising to let people know what you did when they get into town.","e":["Each character loses 5 gold","Gain 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice."]}],[{"n":"You apologize curtly and continue on your way. The Valraths seem disappointed and don't take the news well. You can hear them whispering things to each other as you walk away.","e":["Lose 1 reputation with your highest-reputation faction.","Scenario: start with Curse"]}]],
    48: [[{"n":"You give the farmer a moment to say goodbye, then lead him away and complete the deed. The farmer thanks you for your kindness, wiping away a tear.","e":["Each character gains 2 XP","Scenario: start with Safeguard"]}],[{"c":"Any character can perform a heal of value > 2 targeting an ally","n":"You set to work on the kivak, patching the wounds. Slowly, slowly, the beast turns its head, then calms its breathing, finally coming to a shaky standing position. It licks at you, nuzzling its horn against your face. The farmer couldn't be happier at your assistance.\n\n\"Thank you! You have no idea what this means to me, thank you! I'll never let you stray again!\"","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)","Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"o":1,"n":"You attempt to heal the beast, but it is too far gone from its fall. It flails as you try to comfort it, and in its demise, it lashes out at anyone nearby. You do what you can to give it a dignified end, soothing the pain as best you can. The farmer thanks you for your trouble, then asks to be left to mourn.","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]}]],
    49: [[{"n":"\"Yes, that's it! Matrimony is the perfect conclusion to a tale of tragedy. I can picture the knowing nods of the audience now!\" He scurries back to Gloomhaven to perform the ballad immediately.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]}],[{"n":"Basseloff runs his tongue along his teeth, thinking through the words. Finally, he gives a slow nod that turns more enthusiastic as it goes on.\n\n\"A tragedy must end in death, and your proposed—well, my inspired conclusion, really—drives home the random, senseless violence that can snuff the flame of life at any time. A fitting finish!\" He rushes back to Gloomhaven to perform the song immediately.","e":["Scenario: start with Ward"]}],[{"n":"Basseloff scrunches up his nose, processing your attempt at concluding his ballad. Slowly, curiously, an eyebrow raises, soon matched by the other—his face is the picture of surprise. \"Yes! That's it! A break from troachic octameter is precisely what's needed to disarm my audience, to stun them into the muddled immobilization of the mind, this poisoned wound is the curse of my genius! You are made brilliant by virtue of my catalytic muse, and I thank you!\" He hurries back to Gloomhaven to perform the masterpiece immediately.","e":["Scenario: start with Safeguard"]}]],
    50: [[{"e":["Gain 5 collective gold for each item you retrieved."]},{"t":["armored"],"c":"Trait: Armored","e":["Treat the negative effects below as if you retrieved 3 fewer items."]},{"c":"0 items","e":["Scenario: start with Curse","Lose 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]},{"c":"1 item","e":["No effect"]},{"c":"2 items","e":["Scenario: start with Wound"]},{"c":"3 items","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Discard 1"]},{"c":"4 items","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Discard 1"]},{"c":"5 or more items","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Discard 2"]},{"c":"Retrieved the child","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Merchant Guild"]},{"c":"Retrieved all items","n":"\"Thank you so much, truly. You could have been a bit quicker, of course, and that would certainly have an impact on the condition of these things,\" the merchant holds up the rug, which is pocked with numerous holes, \"but we appreciate your help all the same.\"","e":["Gain 10 additional collective gold"]}]],
    51: [[{"c":"Pay 10 collective gold","n":"You purchase a lucky acorn, tucking it into your pocket. There's probably nothing to it, but you can't help but feel that some force out there is looking out for you.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]}],[{"c":"Pay 15 collective gold","n":"You purchase a lucky acorn, tucking it into your pocket. There's probably nothing to it, but you can't help but feel that some force out there is looking out for you.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]}],[{"n":"You pass by the stand without purchasing anything. She calls after you: \"If you change your mind, be sure to stop back by!\"","e":["No effect"]}]],
    52: [[{"c":"Pay 15 collective gold","n":"You hand over the coins, and she passes you the potion. \"Mother always said the products pick the people. You're good people.\"","e":["Gain item 45 Major Element Potion","Scenario: start with Safeguard"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"Mother always said money makes friends. Let's be friends someday, eh?\"","e":["No effect"],"r":1}],[{"t":["persuasive","educated"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive or Educated","n":"\"Fancy talk, fancy people! Mother always said the best off are always looking for the most off.\"","e":["Apply outcome A","Increase the amount lost by 5 gold."]},{"o":1,"n":"The Vermling will not accept the tiny sum you offer.","e":["No effect"],"r":1}]],
    53: [[{"n":"The man directs you to the top of a nearby mountain. It's an arduous journey that puts you two days through thorn-filled paths to reach the crest, where you find a solid stone slab. Hours of back-breaking labor later, you've broken the stone and recovered a handsome chest full of gold and fist-sized rubies.\n\nYou make your way back down and the old man is waiting for you. \"Told you it'd be worth the trouble! Now, let's see about my share.\"","e":["Choose to gain between 0 and 40 collective gold (giving the rest to the old man). If you collectively gained more than 25 gold, each character starts the next scenario with curse.","Scenario: start with Wound"]},{"t":["strong"],"c":"Trait: Strong","e":["Each character gains 10 additional gold"]}],[{"n":"\"Alright, alright. An even split it is.\"\n\nThe man directs you to the top of a nearby mountain. It's an arduous journey that puts you two days through thorn-filled paths to reach the crest, where you find a solid stone slab. Hours of back-breaking labor later, you've broken the stone and recovered a handsome chest full of gold and fist-sized rubies.\n\nYou make your way back down and the old man is waiting for you. \"Told you it'd be worth the trouble! Now let's see about my share.\"","e":["Scenario: start with Wound","Gain 20 collective gold"]},{"t":["strong"],"c":"Trait: Strong","e":["Each character gains 10 additional gold"]}]],
    54: [[{"n":"You sit in the middle of the road, exhale a long breath, and wait for the world to point the way to your goals. Hours pass, and still you wait. Disturbing your patience, a dragonfly lands on your fingertip. Your eyes flutter open, and in that moment, you understand. The intention is right, but the place... the place is wrong. You pack your things and head off.","e":["Event card road 55"]}],[{"n":"Words have power, so lots of words very quickly should be exceptionally powerful. You babble incoherent phrases, casting them out of your mouth like arcane barbs. The bugs around you take no notice. You redouble your efforts. You can taste the power, and you will harness it for your own.\n\nHours later, the sun begins to set, and still you cry for strength. Then you spot them—a set of insects crawling out from under a rock. You don't know where their eyes are, but you can tell they are making eye contact with you. You. Are. Heard.\n\nYou scoop them up for a closer look, and they scuttle up your arm and into your ears. You feel fuzzy.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle","Each character may start the next scenario in any empty hex within 3 hexes of a starting hex but suffers damage X, where X is equal to their range to the nearest starting hex."]}]],
    55: [[{"n":"You sit in the middle of the road, exhale a long breath, and wait for the world to point the way to your goals. Hours pass, and still you wait. The words are on the tip of your tongue, but they're not ready to be spoken.","e":["Check one box below, or two if a character has arcane.","Tick a box"]}],[{"n":"Words have power, and your attention to the underlying ether of the world has paid off. Your mouth opens, and without any conscious control, out fall words that have not been spoken since before recorded history. The ground bubbles like a living carpet...\n\nIf you have no boxes checked in Outcome A above, read 79.3.\n\nIf you have 1-3 boxes checked in Outcome A above, read 104.3.\n\nIf you have all four boxes checked in Outcome A above, read 69.4.","e":["If you have no boxes checked in Outcome A above.: Read section 79.3.","If you have 1-3 boxes checked in Outcome A above.: Read section 104.3.","If you have all four boxes checked in Outcome A above.: Read section 69.4."]}]],
    56: [[{"n":"\"Perfect! As the first field test participants ever, I'll ask that you record every detail. How comfortable it was, how safe you felt knowing you had the highest technology probability adjuster available, whether there's other color options you'd prefer, that kind of thing.\"","e":["Gain 5 collective gold","Select one character to add two minus1 cards to their attack modifier deck for the next scenario.","The monster modifier deck starts the next scenario with bless"]},{"c":"Successfully complete the scenario","e":["section 19.2.","Gain 2 battle goal checkmark(s)"]}],[{"n":"You drape the pulsing necklaces of heavy tubes and metal around your neck. \"Perfect! As the first field test participants ever, I'll ask that you record every detail. How comfortable it was, how safe you felt, if it accidentally siphoned off negative energy from your adversaries, and so on.\"","e":["Each character gains 5 gold","Each character adds two minus1 cards to their attack modifier deck for the next scenario.","The monster modifier deck starts the next scenario with two bless cards."]},{"c":"Successfully complete the scenario","e":["section 19.2.","Gain 2 battle goal checkmark(s)"]}]],
    57: [[{"t":["strong","nimble","armored"],"c":"Trait: Strong or Nimble or Armored","n":"With some deft action, you're able to break free of the root-like vines wrapping around your feet. Exhausted, you turn to face the woman, but she's already gone.","e":["Discard 2"]},{"o":1,"n":"You hack at the vines underfoot, but for each one you cut, two more seem to sprout. They wrap their way around your boots and snake up your legs, pulling you towards the ground. The woman is long gone by the time you wriggle out.","e":["Discard 3"]}],[{"n":"You attempt to dive towards the woman, but the root-like vines have wrapped your legs and are actively pulling you into the earth. The woman turns to leave as you are drawn down to your neck in the moss-covered ground. It takes hours of wriggling to free yourself.","e":["Discard 3"]}],[{"n":"You drop your weapons as a sign of respect, and the old woman silently recalls the roots into the earth. With a subtle shrug, she invites you to share a meal of root vegetables, wordlessly enjoying the company. Before you leave, she rubs each of your weapons with a purple vegetable, then wanders off into the forest. Strange.","e":["During the first round of the next scenario, each character adds poison to all of their attacks performed."]}]],
    58: [[{"n":"You hand off the potion and point out which way the Silent Knife ran. The guard thanks you for your help and rushes off in hot pursuit.","e":["Lose item 45 Major Element Potion","Gain 1 reputation with Military","Event card road 60","Lose trait: Friend Of The Silent Knife"]}],[{"t":["persuasive"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive","n":"You spin a long-winded yarn about how a brigand held you at dagger-point, threatening your life, then ran off to the right. You watch the guard sprint off, knowing full well your friend went left.","e":["Event card road 60"]},{"o":1,"n":"Under pressure, you point in the first wrong direction you can think of: the way he just came from. \"Empty your bags!\" he orders. He confiscates the potion and writes you a written notice of a court date.","e":["Lose item 45 Major Element Potion","Lose 1 reputation with Military","Event card city 40","Event card road 60"]}],[{"n":"Two quick blows is all it takes, then it's a simple matter to dispose of them in a spot they won't be found. The Silent Knife owes you one.","e":["Event card road 60"]}]],
    59: [[{"c":"Trait Friend of The Silent Knife is present","n":"\"Well, if it isn't my old crew.\" The Silent Knife, still clad in dark leather armor, leaps down from a svelte-looking horse and comes over to greet you. \"You know what? This lot gets a pass.\"\n\nThe Silent Knife winks at you and whispers. \"Sorry for the scare. I just slum it with these guys for some entertainment between jobs.\"","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"\"Huh, not ringing a bell, somehow. Now turn over your gold!\"","e":["Apply outcome B"]}],[{"n":"You see the bandits form up, and you mount your strike. Some are scared off by your ferocity, but others engage you hungrily. The Silent Knife throws a few good daggers, too, before they ride off.","e":["Scenario: suffer 2 damage","Scenario: start with Poison"]}]],
    60: [[{"n":"\"Oh, it's beautiful. Even better than I remembered, thank you so much for keeping it safe for me. You're really the perfect crew, shame I'm retired.\" The Silent Knife looks up for a moment, then snaps their fingers. \"Ah! I found something else I thought you'd like.\"","e":["Lose item 45 Major Element Potion","Gain a random item design","Scenario: start with Safeguard"]}],[{"n":"You explain that, while you would help under other circumstances, you won't be able to return the potion to them.\n\n\"Sure, right. I see how it is. I thought I was pretty clear that I was going to come back 'round for it, and that I was just giving it to you for safekeeping. But that's fine, I'll be more careful about where I place my trust in the future.\"","e":["Lose trait: Friend Of The Silent Knife"]}]],
    61: [[{"n":"You kneel, and the Automatic King's jaw lilts open with a bit of a giggle. \"Do you pledge to serve the Automatic King and carry out his... uh, decrees?\" You nod, and the Automatic King is pleased. \"Then rise, my knights!\"\n\nThere's a pause, then the jaw of the Automatic King creaks open again. \"Also, turn around and close your eyes, because I want to give you something to show you're my knights.\" You do so. \"And don't peek!\" You hear some scrambling behind you, and a moment later, the Automatic King speaks again. \"Open your eyes, and receive thy knightly armor!\"\n\n\"Do good stuff in my name. Okay, bye!\"","e":["Gain item 18 Heavy Basinet"]}],[{"n":"You refuse to play along with this nonsense distraction, and anyone who launches an arrow at you needs to feel the consequences. As soon as you get close enough, a group of Vermling children scurry out of all manner of places, rushing up the hillside and back towards whatever home they come from. With the automaton cleared out, it's a simple matter to investigate the ruined machine, and after prying open some panels, you discover scrap you can salvage.","e":["Gain 10 collective gold"]}]],
    62: [[{"n":"You recognize the crystals as the product of an Orchid inosculation ceremony, where two Orchids who have pledged their lives in union remove the entirety of their crystal growths and combine them with their partner's, planting the result. If left undisturbed, this once-in-a-lifetime ritual may produce offspring. You put the earth back on top of them and move on, pleased to have witnessed it.","e":["Scenario: start with Ward"]}],[{"t":["orchid","educated"],"c":"Trait: Orchid or Educated","e":["Apply outcome A"]},{"o":1,"n":"You dig up the crystals and stash them in your pack—they may be evidence of a crime, or at the very least, worth something to someone. Partway to your destination, though, you smell the unmistakable retch of mold—the crystals have taken on water and are dripping a foul-smelling liquid. You discard them by the side of the road and vow to buy a new bag when you return to the city.","e":["Scenario: start with Curse"]}]],
    63: [[{"n":"In their blood rage, your old party member can't determine who is friend or foe. You take as many blows in the chaos as the guards, but the guards eventually fall. You call out, but the Berserker wastes no time disappearing into the nearby forest. One of the guards looks to still be alive, albeit missing a hand."},{"e":["To finish the job, read section 18.1."]},{"e":["To let the guard live, read section 90.2."]}],[{"n":"It was a brutal and bloody fight, but with your help, the guards subdue the Berserker. After the blood rage wears off, your old friend collapses from exhaustion.\n\nThe guard thanks you. \"That was brutal! This Inox just went into an all-out rage—but I think we've learned a lesson today about insulting someone's horns. Right?\" The guard looks over to a member of his squad, now newly missing an arm and trying to bandage the remains.\n\n\"Right, sir. Yes.\" The guardsman clasps the unconscious Berserker in irons and starts dragging your old friend back towards Gloomhaven. Seems they missed collecting one of the Berserker's axes, and after prying it out of the femur it was lodged in, you think it could still see some use.","e":["Gain 1 reputation with Military","Scenario: suffer 2 damage","Gain item 138 Bloody Axe"]}]],
    64: [[{"n":"Conversation becomes awkward, and you ask to be let out at the side of the road. The Berserker gives you a big grin. \"Want to walk the rest, huh? Well, see you soon!\" You nod politely.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"t":["chaotic","outcast"],"c":"Trait: Chaotic or Outcast","n":"You pull out the axe and show it to the Berserker. \"I thought of all people... He insulted me, to my face! There are consequences, y'know?\" The Berserker's volume is increasing, suggesting there is going to be a full-on rage soon.\n\nYou agree that without repercussions, civility can't exist. The Berserker nods along, assured there's finally someone who understands. You're dropped off just beside your destination and your murderous companion departs with a cheerful wave. \"Keep the axe! I can afford a nicer one now!\"You agree that without repercussions, civility can't exist. The Berserker nods along, assured there's finally someone who understands. You're dropped off just beside your destination and your murderous companion departs with a cheerful wave. \"Keep the axe! I can afford a nicer one now!\"","e":["Scenario: start with Safeguard","Gain item 34 Battle Axe"]},{"o":1,"n":"You pull out the axe and show it to the Berserker. \"I thought of all people... He insulted me, to my face! There are consequences, y'know?\" The Berserker's volume is increasing, suggesting there is going to be a full-on rage soon.\n\nThe pressure builds: \"It was easier when we traveled together—no one questioned the lives we took. Suddenly, I'm at fault? Get out!\" You hastily exit the wagon, and the axe is tossed out the window a moment later. It's an exhausting hike the rest of the way.","e":["Discard 2","Gain item 34 Battle Axe"]}]],
    65: [[{"n":"\"Trade is good for all parties, and the success reaches far. We will consider your recommendation strongly.\"","e":["Gain 1 prosperity"]}],[{"n":"The Vermling nods. \"Then our fears are true. These Orchids are not to be trusted. We will see to it their delegates pay the price when we next meet.\" The Vermling unfolds a crude drawing of something you haven't seen before.\n\n\"For you, for your honesty. Our technology may be unfamiliar to you, but it has its purpose.\"","e":["Gain a random item design"]}]],
    66: [[{"n":"You shout out to the voice in the trees, asking for safe passage. \"Cease your speech. We will confer.\" There is a moment's peace, and after a few minutes, you feel the heat at the base of your neck subside. Out steps your old friend the Doomstalker.\n\n\"Friends! It is you! My charge believed you enemies, but that could not be further from the truth. Thus, she will atone by being your guide.\" The Doomstalker pushes a young Orchid girl forward. She is holding a solid bow and looks sheepish as she greets you.\n\n\"Sorry for assuming the worst. I'll take you through our lands.\" You thank your old friend, and press on.","e":["Scenario: start with Safeguard"]}],[{"n":"With forward momentum, you make it to the tree line, but your adversary presses the attack. They give chase and the hunt begins, with arrow after arrow slowing your progress. Eventually, you cross a stream and the pursuit stops: you must have finally left their territory. You'll find a different path next time.","e":["Scenario: suffer 3 damage"],"r":1}],[{"n":"You throw your hands up and step slowly back out the way you came. It takes longer than you'd like, but eventually the heat at the base of your neck subsides.","e":["Draw another event card"],"r":1}]],
    67: [[{"n":"The Savvas demonstrates techniques, tips, and methods you'd only pick up after making those mistakes yourself. You finish the training session exhausted but pleased.","e":["Each character gains 15 XP","Lose 5xC collective gold"]}],[{"c":"C collective masteries completed","n":"You mop the floor with this indignant Savvas, leaving part of its jaw cracked open. It laughs. \"Maybe the Elementalist really was a good judge of character... not bad.\"","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)","Each character gains 5 XP"]},{"o":1,"n":"The old Savvas wipes the floor with you, and you wince whenever you think of it for some time.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]}],[{"c":"C-1 collective masteries completed","n":"You handily mop the floor with this indignant Savvas, leaving part of its jaw cracked open. \"Heh, maybe you're a two-hander after all. Not bad, I see what the Elementalist saw in you.\"","e":["Gain 1 battle goal checkmark(s)"]},{"o":1,"n":"The old Savvas wipes the floor with you, and you wince whenever you think of it for some time.","e":["Scenario: start with Muddle"]}]],
    68: [[{"n":"It doesn't take long to find the shepherd—the hundreds of kivak following behind him was a dead giveaway. \"Ho there! Is that Grump? Grump, what are you doing way out here?\" You explain, and the shepherd gives you his thanks. \"We wander out around these parts, far and wide. If it'd be useful to you, you can take one of them along for your trip. Not Grump, obviously, he'll need some time to heal up. But they're good for carrying you and your companions.\"","e":["At the start of the next scenario, designate an empty hex that can be reached by performing move 3 from a starting hex. Characters may choose to start in that hex or an empty hex adjacent to it instead of a starting hex.","Event card road 69"]}],[{"n":"You bandage the kivak's leg and it dutifully follows you towards your destination, stopping periodically to graze on wildflowers. Keeping track of it is exhausting, but perhaps this beast can help you.","e":["At the start of the next scenario, designate an empty hex that can be reached by performing move 3 from a starting hex. Characters may choose to start in that hex or an empty hex adjacent to it instead of a starting hex.","Discard 1"]},{"c":"Successfully complete the scenario","e":["Rread section 110.5."]}]],
    69: [[{"c":"Pay 5 collective gold","n":"\"There you are, this is the finest kivak in the herd that also happened to be the closest one when you asked for one. It'll carry you along. No need to bring 'im back, they always find their way eventually.\"","e":["At the start of the next scenario, designate an empty hex that can be reached by performing move 3 from a starting hex. Characters may choose to start in that hex or an empty hex adjacent to it instead of a starting hex."]},{"o":1,"n":"\"Sorry, can't just let them run off for free, got a lot of mouths to feed.\" You watch the herd of kivak eating everything nearby, from grass to rocks. \"They're not picky, but I sure am.\"","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"The shepherd gives a loud three-note whistle, and up wanders Grump, the kivak you rescued. \"Grump's been talking a lot about you, probably. I wouldn't know, I don't speak kivak. Sometimes feel like I could though, eh?\"\n\nGrump takes the opportunity to nuzzle into your hand, then wanders back to its herd.","e":["Scenario: start with Bless"]}]],
    70: [[{"n":"You quickly pack up your camp and push your belongings through the rift, following close behind. You don't know what awaits you on the other side, but if the Soultether needs help, you're there.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen","Unlock scenario 94","New Scenario: A Watery Rescue 94. This scenario must be played immediately."]}],[{"n":"You mark the location of the rift down and promise to return when you're ready. The jellyfish thrashes a bit and dries up dead by the time the sun peeks above the mountainside.","e":["Scenario: start with Curse","Unlock scenario 94","Event card city 85"]}]],
    71: [[{"n":"You step through the ragged tear in reality. Your insides stretch to vibrant jelly, your bones looping in on themselves. It is not altogether unpleasant, and you can't help but remember fish exist and that shoes can fit on hands even though they aren't intended to. What a strange notion, that we care so much about where clothes are worn even though death is watching and you can see language painted in books.\n\nWith a silence that nearly ruptures your eardrums, you arrive at your destination. You look around, calm, but the Nightshroud is nowhere to be seen. It seems like it was a success—ah, there's the splitting, stomach-churning headache you'd expect.","e":["Scenario: start with Immobilize"]}],[{"n":"\"A spool of string can roll forever, until it snaps.\" The Nightshroud nods, as though it understands something important. \"You have so many faces, but I will remember.\"\n\nA cloud passes, casting the valley into darkness. You look closely, but the Nightshroud is gone.","e":["No effect"]}]],
    72: [[{"n":"Knowing better than to get too close to the machinations of the Plagueherald, you keep a wide berth between you and the corpses and continue down the road.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"t":["immunity"],"c":"Trait: Immunity","n":"You rifle through the corpses, grabbing stray coins and valuables as you go. The sight is sickening, and while you don't feel physically ill, you do feel a certain dark pall in the air.","e":["Scenario: start with Curse","Gain 10 collective gold","Event card city 90"]},{"o":1,"n":"You make off with a good haul, but start feeling sick as soon as you're done.","e":["Scenario: start with Poison","Gain 10 collective gold","Gain trait: Immunity"]}],[{"n":"You gather tinder and approach the corpses as close as good sense will allow. They alight as though fueled by some unseen gas, inflating and spluttering as they burn. The ash is oppressive in the air and fills your lungs with a stinging sensation, but you take some comfort in knowing you stopped the spread to other local fauna.\n\nIf you already have IMMUNITY, add event C-90 to the city deck.","e":["Gain trait: Immunity","Event card city 90"]}]],
    73: [[{"n":"\"For you, anything!\" The Quartermaster is happy to give you some supplies for your next battle.","e":["At the end of the first round of the next scenario, each character may recover one lost item."]}],[{"n":"\"I purchase everything wholesale, and I'm happy to extend those discounts on to you.\"","e":["Each character may immediately purchase one item from the available item supply as though its cost was five gold less and your reputation with each faction was two greater."]}]],
    74: [[{"n":"\"Wonderous! My melodies should give you the confidence you require!\" From the very first pluck of the lute, you can tell you'll regret this.","e":["Scenario: start with Strengthen","Each character adds two minus1 cards to their attack modifier deck for the next scenario."]},{"e":["Successfully complete the scenario: Read section 35.5.","Lose 1 reputation with any one faction of your choice."]}],[{"t":["persuasive"],"c":"Trait: Persuasive","n":"You convince Basseloff that tagging along with you would be a terrible bore. \"You're right, I require a more valiant mission to best recharge my depleted muse. Good day!\"","e":["No effect"]},{"o":1,"n":"You try to explain why it's a bad idea to come on this mission, but Basseloff is having none of it. \"Hogwash! In any case, you are sure to die without my assistance. I won't hear another word of it.\"\n\nHe falls in line beside you, a determined grit underneath his perfectly-pressed blouse.\n\nRead Outcome A.","e":["Apply outcome A"]}]],
    75: [[{"n":"Without much difficulty, you step around the trap and continue on your way.","e":["No effect"]}],[{"n":"With the least surprising snap of all time, the jaws clamp down, piercing your leg. It takes some doing, but you manage to pry it off and continue on your way.","e":["The character who stepped on the trap starts the next scenario with immobilize and wound.","Scenario: start with Muddle"]}]],
    76: [[{"n":"The Bladeswarm doesn't acknowledge your request, but as you begin to leave, a vanguard of insects advance in front of you. \"Do not die, you will be needed.\".","e":["At the start of the next scenario, choose one revealed monster to gain immobilize."]}],[{"n":"The Bladeswarm waves an arm and a stream of insects falls to the ground, scuttling to follow you. \"We will assist. May you mount an overwhelming offensive.\"","e":["At the start of the next scenario, choose one revealed monster to gain wound and poison."]}]],
    77: [[{"n":"The Bladeswarm makes a conscious effort to nod. \"I will purchase all you can produce.\"","e":["You may sell any number of potions for 20 gold each."]}],[{"n":"\"Then I will depart.\" You watch as the Bladeswarm discards its cloak and dissolves back into thousands of crawling legs and mandibles. Rather than mounting the hristek, though, it swells underneath its hooves, lifting it and conveying the confused animal down the road like a mobile black carpet. Perhaps it still has more to learn about modern society.","e":["No effect"]}]],
  },
};
